{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01FG5VLcYfBD1DZmLgnDuFbQ","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Paper Framing: Diagnostic Analysis of Temporal Abstraction in World-Model RL\n2\t\n3\t## Title Candidates\n4\t\n5\t1. **\"Why Temporal Abstraction Fails in World-Model Reinforcement Learning: A Diagnostic Analysis\"**\n6\t2. **\"The Delusional Critic Problem in Variable-Rate Imagination\"**\n7\t3. **\"Diagnosing Value Overestimation in Temporally-Abstract World Models\"**\n8\t\n9\t## Venue\n10\t\n11\t**CoRL 2026** — Deadline: 2026-05-29\n12\t\n13\t## Narrative Positioning\n14\t\n15\tThis is a **diagnostic analysis paper**, not a method paper. We do not propose a new algorithm. Instead, we provide a systematic, controlled investigation answering: *Why does temporal abstraction fail in world-model RL?*\n16\t\n17\tThe contribution is a **closed causal chain** from mechanism to failure mode, backed by a factorial experiment design that isolates each factor. Diagnostic papers are valued when they (a) address a widely-attempted but poorly-understood failure, (b) provide actionable insight for future method design, and (c) are methodologically rigorous.\n18\t\n19\t---\n20\t\n21\t## Core Claims\n22\t\n23\t### C1: Variable-rate imagination in DreamerV3 consistently degrades performance\n24\t\n25\tTemporal abstraction via variable dt—whether learned or fixed—degrades asymptotic performance relative to the dt=1 baseline across all tested configurations.\n26\t\n27\t| Evidence | Experiment | Key Metric |\n28\t|----------|-----------|------------|\n29\t| Baseline stability | exp_001_baseline (dt=1) | Stable convergence ~950 eval return |\n30\t| Fixed dt=2 collapse | exp_006_fixed_dt2 (dt=2, subsample ON, H=15) | Peak 485@35K → collapse to ~135@65K |\n31\t| Fixed dt=4 severe degradation | exp_007_fixed_dt4 (dt=4) | Peak 176.9@25K, 144.4@45K (33% of baseline@45K=443) |\n32\t| Learned gate collapse | exp_005 (learned gate) | Peak 541@55K → 99@145K |\n33\t\n34\t**Strength**: Strong. Three independent dt>1 configurations all show degradation. No positive result exists for variable-rate imagination in our setup.\n35\t\n36\t### C2: Trained dt_embedding causes delusional critic (root cause)\n37\t\n38\t**⚠️ Causal attribution pending**: Current 008c vs 008d comparison confounds dt_embedding training with RSSM training data composition (subsample ON/OFF). exp_008f (dt_embed_dim=0 + subsample ON + dt=2 imagination + H=8) will isolate the dt_embedding variable. C2 strength is provisional until 008f completes.\n39\t\n40\tThe trained dt_embedding enables precise dt prediction in imagination, but RSSM state prediction quality at dt>1 is insufficient to support this precision. The result is systematic value overestimation (delusional critic) that drives actor learning toward incorrect policies.\n41\t\n42\t| Evidence | Experiment | Key Metric |\n43\t|----------|-----------|------------|\n44\t| Untrained dt_emb, no collapse | exp_008c (dt=2, subsample OFF, untrained dt_emb, H=8) | eval plateau ~242@55K; v/e: @35K=21.8% (0.90x) → @55K=29.1% (0.72x) → @65K=32.8% (0.58x) (declining normalized v/e, ~7x slower than trained) |\n45\t| Trained dt_emb, collapse | exp_008d (dt=2, subsample ON, trained dt_emb, H=8) | eval declining 167→146→141 @25K→35K→45K; v/e: @25K=15.5% (1.78x) → @35K=41.2% (1.71x) → @45K=69.3% (2.09x) (accelerating overestimation) |\n46\t| Both trained dt_emb → accelerating v/e | exp_006 (H=15) vs exp_008d (H=8) | 006: v/e @35K=31.1% (1.29x)→@45K=53.3% (1.61x)→@55K=93.3% (2.31x); 008d: v/e @35K=41.2% (1.71x)→@45K=69.3% (2.09x) — both show accelerating normalized v/e leading to collapse |\n47\t| Baseline v/e calibration (overshoot reference) | exp_001_baseline | v/e@35K=24.1%, @45K=33.1%, @55K=40.4%. Overshoot ratio: 008d@35K=1.7x, @45K=2.1x; 006@45K=1.6x, @55K=2.3x (all >1.5x = pathological) |\n48\t\n49\t**Strength**: Strong. The 008c vs 008d comparison is a controlled experiment isolating dt_embedding training as the single variable. The v/e overshoot ratio (experiment v/e / baseline v/e at same step) quantitatively identifies pathological regimes: trained dt_emb variants exceed 1.5x baseline before collapse, while untrained variants stay at or below baseline levels. **Pending confirmation**: exp_008f (dt_embed_dim=0 + subsample ON) will isolate whether dt_embedding conditioning or RSSM's learned dt=2 dynamics is the true cause.\n50\t\n51\t### C3: Untrained dt_embedding prevents optimistic drift, substantively protecting performance\n52\t\n53\tWhen dt_embedding is untrained (random fixed), the value function cannot exploit precise dt information, preventing the optimistic value drift seen in trained variants. This value growth suppression substantively protects performance: exp_008a demonstrates two complete V-shaped recovery cycles over 105K steps (peak @105K=778, 85% of baseline 916), with normalized v/e consistently suppressed at 0.59-0.93x baseline. The trained dt_embedding variant (exp_006) collapses catastrophically as its v/e ratio accelerates far past baseline levels (2.3x baseline@55K).\n54\t\n55\t| Evidence | Experiment | Key Metric |\n56\t|----------|-----------|------------|\n57\t| Two V-shaped recoveries (105K) | exp_008a (dt=2, subsample OFF, untrained dt_emb, H=15) | 501→563→488→608→470→584→572→778; two complete recovery cycles over 105K steps. @65K=608 (-1.3% baseline), @105K=778 (-15.1% baseline, 85% of 916). No collapse. |\n58\t| Sustained v/e suppression | exp_008a | v/e: 37.6%@55K → 37.2%@65K → 53.6%@75K → 47.5%@85K → 49.7%@95K → 38.6%@105K. Normalized v/e: 0.93x→0.66x→0.75x→0.68x→0.79x→0.59x baseline. Consistently below 1.0x, no acceleration. |\n59\t| Trained dt_emb: accelerating collapse | exp_006 (dt=2, subsample ON, trained dt_emb, H=15) | 485→477→360→collapse; v/e: 53.3%@45K (1.61x)→93.3%@55K (2.31x) → immediate collapse |\n60\t| v/e rate comparison (H=8 controlled) | exp_008c vs exp_008d | 008c (untrained): @35K=21.8% (0.90x)→@65K=32.8% (0.58x) (normalized declining); 008d (trained): @25K=15.5% (1.78x)→@35K=41.2% (1.71x) (normalized >1.5x = pathological). ~7x slower overestimation rate |\n61\t| Baseline v/e calibration | exp_001_baseline | v/e: 8.7%@25K → 24.1%@35K → 40.4%@55K → 56.3%@65K → 65.6%@105K (stable 69-72% from 135K+). 008a normalized v/e: 0.93x@55K → 0.66x@65K → 0.59x@105K (suppressed, diverging further below baseline); 008d: 1.7x@35K → 2.1x@45K (optimistic drift) |\n62\t\n63\t**Strength**: Strong (B+ confirmed with 105K long-run data). Two complete V-shaped recovery cycles (501→608→470→778) with normalized v/e consistently 0.59-0.93x baseline across 105K steps. This is structural value growth suppression, not a transient delay. Contrasts sharply with exp_006's accelerating v/e (1.6x→2.3x baseline → collapse). The mechanism is clear: untrained dt_embedding prevents the value function from exploiting precise (but wrong) dt>1 predictions, suppressing the optimistic value drift that drives the delusional critic feedback loop in trained variants.\n64\t\n65\t**Diagnostic metric: v/e overshoot ratio** = experiment v/e / baseline v/e at same training step. >1.5x = pathological warning. Trained dt_emb variants: 008d@35K=1.7x, @45K=2.1x; 006@45K=1.6x, @55K=2.3x. Untrained: 008a normalized v/e range 0.59-0.93x over 55K-105K (consistently below baseline = healthy, diverging further from baseline over time).\n66\t\n67\t**105K long-run confirmed**: exp_008a ran to 112K steps. Normalized v/e at 105K=0.59x baseline (lowest point), confirming value growth suppression is structural, not a transient delay. The suppression strengthens over time rather than converging to baseline levels.\n68\t\n69\t### C4: Longer dt amplifies the problem\n70\t\n71\tIncreasing dt from 2 to 4 worsens degradation, consistent with RSSM prediction error compounding over longer temporal gaps.\n72\t\n73\t| Evidence | Experiment | Key Metric |\n74\t|----------|-----------|------------|\n75\t| dt=2 degradation | exp_006_fixed_dt2 | Peak 485, collapse to ~135 |\n76\t| dt=4 severe degradation | exp_007_fixed_dt4 | Peak 176.9@25K, 144.4@45K (33% of baseline@45K=443) |\n77\t| Monotonic relationship | dt=1 (~950) > dt=2 (peak 485@35K) > dt=4 (peak 177@25K) | Clear monotonic decline |\n78\t\n79\t**Strength**: Moderate. Only two dt values tested (2 and 4). The monotonic trend is clear but a finer grid (dt=3, dt=6) would strengthen this claim. Sufficient for a supporting claim but not a standalone finding.\n80\t\n81\t### C5: Learning signal reduction from shorter effective horizons compounds degradation but is not the root cause\n82\t\n83\tSubsampling with dt>1 reduces the effective number of learning transitions per episode. This contributes to degradation but is neither necessary nor sufficient for collapse.\n84\t\n85\t| Evidence | Experiment | Key Metric |\n86\t|----------|-----------|------------|\n87\t| Subsample OFF, still degraded | exp_008c (subsample OFF, untrained dt_emb, H=8) | eval ~242 vs baseline ~950 |\n88\t| Subsample OFF, no collapse | exp_008a (subsample OFF, untrained dt_emb, H=15) | eval 778@105K (85% baseline), no collapse through 112K steps |\n89\t| Subsample ON, collapse | exp_008d (subsample ON, trained dt_emb, H=8) | eval 146, value overestimation |\n90\t| Horizon effect | exp_008c (H=8) vs exp_008a (H=15) | H=15 significantly outperforms H=8, both subsample OFF |\n91\t\n92\t**Strength**: Moderate. The 008c vs 008a comparison shows horizon length matters independently. But disentangling horizon from subsample effects requires additional controls. The key point—that it's not the root cause—is well-supported by 008c's stability despite lower performance.\n93\t\n94\t---\n95\t\n96\t## Story Arc\n97\t\n98\t### 1. Introduction\n99\t- Temporal abstraction is a long-sought goal in RL (options, macro-actions, skip connections)\n100\t- World-model RL (DreamerV3) offers a natural testbed: modify imagination dt without changing environment interaction\n101\t- Puzzle: all our attempts at variable-rate imagination degrade performance. Why?\n102\t- Contribution: systematic factorial diagnosis identifying trained dt_embedding → delusional critic as the root cause\n103\t\n104\t### 2. Background & Related Work\n105\t- Temporal abstraction in model-free RL (options framework, FiGAR, action repeat)\n106\t- World-model RL (Dreamer family, IRIS, TWM)\n107\t- Variable-rate planning in world models (few prior works, mostly positive framing)\n108\t- Value overestimation / delusional policies in model-based RL\n109\t\n110\t### 3. Methodology\n111\t- DreamerV3 as base architecture\n112\t- Variable-rate imagination: dt_embedding, temporal subsampling, learned gating\n113\t- **Factorial experiment design**: 2×2×2 grid (dt_embedding trained/untrained × subsample ON/OFF × H=8/15) + baselines\n114\t- Diagnostic metrics: eval return, value/eval ratio as overestimation proxy, learning curves\n115\t\n116\t### 4. Results\n117\t- **Finding 1**: All dt>1 configurations degrade (C1)\n118\t- **Finding 2**: Controlled ablation isolates trained dt_embedding (C2) — the \"smoking gun\" comparison (008c vs 008d)\n119\t- **Finding 3**: Untrained dt_embedding prevents optimistic drift, sustaining near-baseline performance (C3)\n120\t- **Finding 4**: Longer dt amplifies (C4)\n121\t- **Finding 5**: Horizon/subsample effects are secondary (C5)\n122\t\n123\t### 5. Discussion\n124\t- Mechanism: why trained dt_embedding causes delusional critic (RSSM fidelity gap at dt>1)\n125\t- Connection to existing theory: delusional policies (Delalleau et al.), model exploitation in MBRL\n126\t- Why this is specific to world-model RL (model-free temporal abstraction doesn't suffer the same failure mode)\n127\t\n128\t### 6. Implications for Future Work\n129\t- Don't train dt_embedding jointly with value function in current world-model architectures\n130\t- RSSM prediction quality must improve before variable-rate imagination is viable\n131\t- Value growth suppression (e.g., untrained dt_embedding) as a potential mitigation direction\n132\t- Need for diagnostic methodology in temporal abstraction research\n133\t\n134\t---\n135\t\n136\t## Anticipated Reviewer Concerns\n137\t\n138\t### R1: \"Limited to one environment / one base algorithm\"\n139\t**Pre-emption**: Our claims are mechanistic (trained dt_embedding → value overestimation → collapse). The causal chain is architecture-specific by design—we diagnose *why* it fails in DreamerV3, not whether it fails everywhere. The mechanism (RSSM fidelity gap) likely generalizes to other latent-dynamics models but we scope claims conservatively.\n140\t**Mitigation**: Cheetah Run is a planned experiment in our experiment schedule, not a stretch goal. We will include at least one additional DMC environment (Cheetah Run) to demonstrate generality of the mechanism.\n141\t\n142\t### R2: \"No proposed solution — what's the actionable takeaway?\"\n143\t**Pre-emption**: Diagnostic papers serve a different purpose than method papers. Identifying root causes (trained dt_embedding) and quantitative signatures (v/e overshoot ratio >1.5x baseline = pathological) gives the community concrete guidance. We explicitly outline mitigation directions (value growth suppression, improved RSSM, decoupled dt_embedding training).\n144\t**Mitigation**: Frame implications section as a \"research agenda\" with specific, testable hypotheses.\n145\t\n146\t### R3: \"Value/eval ratio is a crude proxy for overestimation\"\n147\t**Pre-emption**: We acknowledge this is a proxy, not a formal divergence measure. However, the v/e overshoot ratio (experiment v/e / baseline v/e at same step) consistently identifies pathological overestimation: trained dt_emb variants exceed 1.5x baseline v/e before collapse, while untrained variants stay at or below baseline levels.\n148\t**Mitigation**: Add distributional analysis of value predictions vs. realized returns if time permits.\n149\t\n150\t### R4: \"The factorial design is incomplete — missing cells in the grid\"\n151\t**Pre-emption**: We prioritized the most informative comparisons. The 008c vs 008d pair isolates dt_embedding training with all else held constant—this is the critical controlled experiment.\n152\t**Mitigation**: Explicitly present the factorial grid, mark which cells are filled, and justify the prioritization.\n153\t\n154\t### R5: \"Novelty concern — model exploitation / value overestimation in MBRL is well-known\"\n155\t**Pre-emption**: General MBRL overestimation is known (Janner et al., 2019), but the specific mechanism through temporal abstraction's dt_embedding is novel. Prior work on temporal abstraction in world models has not identified this failure mode. Our contribution is the *specific causal link*, not the general phenomenon.\n156\t\n157\t### R6: \"All results from a single seed — how robust are the conclusions?\"\n158\t**Pre-emption**: Our claims are about *mechanisms* (causal chain from dt_embedding → value overestimation → collapse), not about precise numerical thresholds. The mechanism manifests consistently across all configurations (exp_005, 006, 007, 008d) — four independent experiments all show the same value/eval ratio divergence pattern. The probability of this pattern appearing by chance across 4 experiments is negligible.\n159\t**Mitigation**: Planned multi-seed runs for final paper. The factorial design (008c vs 008d) provides cross-experiment replication of the core mechanism.\n160\t\n161\t### R7: \"The factorial design confounds dt_embedding training with training data composition\"\n162\t**Pre-emption**: We acknowledge this confound between 008c (subsample OFF, untrained dt_emb) and 008d (subsample ON, trained dt_emb). Experiment 008f (dt_embed_dim=0 + subsample ON) is designed to resolve this: it trains with dt=2 transitions (like 008d) but without dt_embedding conditioning. If 008f collapses → the cause is RSSM's learned dt=2 dynamics, not dt_embedding per se. If 008f remains stable → dt_embedding conditioning is confirmed as the root cause.\n163\t**Mitigation**: exp_008f is a blocking experiment for the final paper. Results will be available before submission.\n164\t\n165\t---\n166\t\n167\t## Experiment Coverage Assessment\n168\t\n169\t| Claim | Evidence Status | Gaps |\n170\t|-------|----------------|------|\n171\t| C1 (degradation) | ✅ Strong — 3 configurations (005, 006, 007) all negative | Could add 1 more environment |\n172\t| C2 (root cause: dt_emb) | ⚠️ Provisional — pending exp_008f to resolve dt_embedding vs training data confound | Consider adding value prediction distribution analysis |\n173\t| C3 (preventing optimistic drift) | ✅ Strong (105K confirmed) — 008a@105K=778 (85% baseline), normalized v/e=0.59x, two V-shaped recoveries | None — long-term structural suppression confirmed |\n174\t| C4 (dt amplification) | ⚠️ Moderate — only dt=2 vs dt=4 | Would benefit from dt=3, but not blocking |\n175\t| C5 (horizon/subsample) | ⚠️ Moderate — confounded with other factors | Need 008c-equivalent with H=15 + subsample ON + untrained dt_emb for clean isolation |\n176\t\n177\t### Priority Actions Before Submission\n178\t1. ~~**Check exp_008a@65K**~~ — ✅ Done: 608 (-1.3% baseline), B+ confirmed\n179\t2. **Complete factorial grid analysis** — present all 8 cells, even if some are interpolated\n180\t3. **Value prediction distribution plots** — strengthen C2 beyond ratio proxy\n181\t4. **Second environment** (stretch goal) — addresses R1\n182\t\n183\t---\n184\t\n185\t## Key Figures (Planned)\n186\t\n187\t1. **Figure 1**: Learning curves — all experiments overlaid, showing degradation pattern (hero figure)\n188\t2. **Figure 2**: Value/eval ratio over training — separating healthy vs. pathological regimes\n189\t3. **Figure 3**: Factorial grid summary — 2×2 (dt_emb × subsample) with H as secondary axis\n190\t4. **Figure 4**: Causal diagram — dt_embedding → value overestimation → actor degradation → collapse\n191\t5. **Figure 5**: dt=1 vs dt=2 vs dt=4 comparison — monotonic degradation (C4)\n192\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"c7ee1525-331d-4727-9b3d-5b54e618037d","uuid":"46aa4df8-0ae3-4dcd-b44a-aa58ddfaa508","timestamp":"2026-05-14T06:50:10.152Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0509_9/projects/event-gated-adaptive-horizon/artifacts/dream_reports/dream_20260514T062606/worst/paper_framing.md","content":"# Paper Framing: Diagnostic Analysis of Temporal Abstraction in World-Model RL\n\n## Title Candidates\n\n1. **\"Why Temporal Abstraction Fails in World-Model Reinforcement Learning: A Diagnostic Analysis\"**\n2. **\"The Delusional Critic Problem in Variable-Rate Imagination\"**\n3. **\"Diagnosing Value Overestimation in Temporally-Abstract World Models\"**\n\n## Venue\n\n**CoRL 2026** — Deadline: 2026-05-29\n\n## Narrative Positioning\n\nThis is a **diagnostic analysis paper**, not a method paper. We do not propose a new algorithm. Instead, we provide a systematic, controlled investigation answering: *Why does temporal abstraction fail in world-model RL?*\n\nThe contribution is a **closed causal chain** from mechanism to failure mode, backed by a factorial experiment design that isolates each factor. Diagnostic papers are valued when they (a) address a widely-attempted but poorly-understood failure, (b) provide actionable insight for future method design, and (c) are methodologically rigorous.\n\n---\n\n## Core Claims\n\n### C1: Variable-rate imagination in DreamerV3 consistently degrades performance\n\nTemporal abstraction via variable dt—whether learned or fixed—degrades asymptotic performance relative to the dt=1 baseline across all tested configurations.\n\n| Evidence | Experiment | Key Metric |\n|----------|-----------|------------|\n| Baseline stability | exp_001_baseline (dt=1) | Stable convergence ~950 eval return |\n| Fixed dt=2 collapse | exp_006_fixed_dt2 (dt=2, subsample ON, H=15) | Peak 485@35K → collapse to ~135@65K |\n| Fixed dt=4 severe degradation | exp_007_fixed_dt4 (dt=4) | Peak 176.9@25K, 144.4@45K (33% of baseline@45K=443) |\n| Learned gate collapse | exp_005 (learned gate) | Peak 541@55K → 99@145K |\n\n**Strength**: Strong. Three independent dt>1 configurations all show degradation. No positive result exists for variable-rate imagination in our setup.\n\n### C2: Trained dt_embedding causes delusional critic (root cause)\n\n**⚠️ Causal attribution pending**: Current 008c vs 008d comparison confounds dt_embedding training with RSSM training data composition (subsample ON/OFF). exp_008f (dt_embed_dim=0 + subsample ON + dt=2 imagination + H=8) will isolate the dt_embedding variable. C2 strength is provisional until 008f completes.\n\nThe trained dt_embedding enables precise dt prediction in imagination, but RSSM state prediction quality at dt>1 is insufficient to support this precision. The result is systematic value overestimation (delusional critic) that drives actor learning toward incorrect policies.\n\n| Evidence | Experiment | Key Metric |\n|----------|-----------|------------|\n| Untrained dt_emb, no collapse | exp_008c (dt=2, subsample OFF, untrained dt_emb, H=8) | eval plateau ~242@55K; v/e: @35K=21.8% (0.90x) → @55K=29.1% (0.72x) → @65K=32.8% (0.58x) (declining normalized v/e, ~7x slower than trained) |\n| Trained dt_emb, collapse | exp_008d (dt=2, subsample ON, trained dt_emb, H=8) | eval declining 167→146→141 @25K→35K→45K; v/e: @25K=15.5% (1.78x) → @35K=41.2% (1.71x) → @45K=69.3% (2.09x) (accelerating overestimation) |\n| Both trained dt_emb → accelerating v/e | exp_006 (H=15) vs exp_008d (H=8) | 006: v/e @35K=31.1% (1.29x)→@45K=53.3% (1.61x)→@55K=93.3% (2.31x); 008d: v/e @35K=41.2% (1.71x)→@45K=69.3% (2.09x) — both show accelerating normalized v/e leading to collapse |\n| Baseline v/e calibration (overshoot reference) | exp_001_baseline | v/e@35K=24.1%, @45K=33.1%, @55K=40.4%. Overshoot ratio: 008d@35K=1.7x, @45K=2.1x; 006@45K=1.6x, @55K=2.3x (all >1.5x = pathological) |\n\n**Strength**: Strong. The 008c vs 008d comparison is a controlled experiment isolating dt_embedding training as the single variable. The v/e overshoot ratio (experiment v/e / baseline v/e at same step) quantitatively identifies pathological regimes: trained dt_emb variants exceed 1.5x baseline before collapse, while untrained variants stay at or below baseline levels. **Pending confirmation**: exp_008f (dt_embed_dim=0 + subsample ON) will isolate whether dt_embedding conditioning or RSSM's learned dt=2 dynamics is the true cause.\n\n### C3: Untrained dt_embedding prevents optimistic drift, substantively protecting performance\n\nWhen dt_embedding is untrained (random fixed), the value function cannot exploit precise dt information, preventing the optimistic value drift seen in trained variants. This value growth suppression substantively protects performance: exp_008a demonstrates two complete V-shaped recovery cycles over 105K steps (peak @105K=778, 85% of baseline 916), with normalized v/e consistently suppressed at 0.59-0.93x baseline. The trained dt_embedding variant (exp_006) collapses catastrophically as its v/e ratio accelerates far past baseline levels (2.3x baseline@55K).\n\n| Evidence | Experiment | Key Metric |\n|----------|-----------|------------|\n| Two V-shaped recoveries (105K) | exp_008a (dt=2, subsample OFF, untrained dt_emb, H=15) | 501→563→488→608→470→584→572→778; two complete recovery cycles over 105K steps. @65K=608 (-1.3% baseline), @105K=778 (-15.1% baseline, 85% of 916). No collapse. |\n| Sustained v/e suppression | exp_008a | v/e: 37.6%@55K → 37.2%@65K → 53.6%@75K → 47.5%@85K → 49.7%@95K → 38.6%@105K. Normalized v/e: 0.93x→0.66x→0.75x→0.68x→0.79x→0.59x baseline. Consistently below 1.0x, no acceleration. |\n| Trained dt_emb: accelerating collapse | exp_006 (dt=2, subsample ON, trained dt_emb, H=15) | 485→477→360→collapse; v/e: 53.3%@45K (1.61x)→93.3%@55K (2.31x) → immediate collapse |\n| v/e rate comparison (H=8 controlled) | exp_008c vs exp_008d | 008c (untrained): @35K=21.8% (0.90x)→@65K=32.8% (0.58x) (normalized declining); 008d (trained): @25K=15.5% (1.78x)→@35K=41.2% (1.71x) (normalized >1.5x = pathological). ~7x slower overestimation rate |\n| Baseline v/e calibration | exp_001_baseline | v/e: 8.7%@25K → 24.1%@35K → 40.4%@55K → 56.3%@65K → 65.6%@105K (stable 69-72% from 135K+). 008a normalized v/e: 0.93x@55K → 0.66x@65K → 0.59x@105K (suppressed, diverging further below baseline); 008d: 1.7x@35K → 2.1x@45K (optimistic drift) |\n\n**Strength**: Strong (B+ confirmed with 105K long-run data). Two complete V-shaped recovery cycles (501→608→470→778) with normalized v/e consistently 0.59-0.93x baseline across 105K steps. This is structural value growth suppression, not a transient delay. Contrasts sharply with exp_006's accelerating v/e (1.6x→2.3x baseline → collapse). The mechanism is clear: untrained dt_embedding prevents the value function from exploiting precise (but wrong) dt>1 predictions, suppressing the optimistic value drift that drives the delusional critic feedback loop in trained variants.\n\n**Diagnostic metric: v/e overshoot ratio** = experiment v/e / baseline v/e at same training step. >1.5x = pathological warning. Trained dt_emb variants: 008d@35K=1.7x, @45K=2.1x; 006@45K=1.6x, @55K=2.3x. Untrained: 008a normalized v/e range 0.59-0.93x over 55K-105K (consistently below baseline = healthy, diverging further from baseline over time).\n\n**105K long-run confirmed**: exp_008a ran to 112K steps. Normalized v/e at 105K=0.59x baseline (lowest point), confirming value growth suppression is structural, not a transient delay. The suppression strengthens over time rather than converging to baseline levels.\n\n### C4: Longer dt amplifies the problem\n\nIncreasing dt from 2 to 4 worsens degradation, consistent with RSSM prediction error compounding over longer temporal gaps.\n\n| Evidence | Experiment | Key Metric |\n|----------|-----------|------------|\n| dt=2 degradation | exp_006_fixed_dt2 | Peak 485, collapse to ~135 |\n| dt=4 severe degradation | exp_007_fixed_dt4 | Peak 176.9@25K, 144.4@45K (33% of baseline@45K=443) |\n| Monotonic relationship | dt=1 (~950) > dt=2 (peak 485@35K) > dt=4 (peak 177@25K) | Clear monotonic decline |\n\n**Strength**: Moderate. Only two dt values tested (2 and 4). The monotonic trend is clear but a finer grid (dt=3, dt=6) would strengthen this claim. Sufficient for a supporting claim but not a standalone finding.\n\n### C5: Learning signal reduction from shorter effective horizons compounds degradation but is not the root cause\n\nSubsampling with dt>1 reduces the effective number of learning transitions per episode. This contributes to degradation but is neither necessary nor sufficient for collapse.\n\n| Evidence | Experiment | Key Metric |\n|----------|-----------|------------|\n| Subsample OFF, still degraded | exp_008c (subsample OFF, untrained dt_emb, H=8) | eval ~242 vs baseline ~950 |\n| Subsample OFF, no collapse | exp_008a (subsample OFF, untrained dt_emb, H=15) | eval 778@105K (85% baseline), no collapse through 112K steps |\n| Subsample ON, collapse | exp_008d (subsample ON, trained dt_emb, H=8) | eval 146, value overestimation |\n| Horizon effect | exp_008c (H=8) vs exp_008a (H=15) | H=15 significantly outperforms H=8, both subsample OFF |\n\n**Strength**: Moderate. The 008c vs 008a comparison shows horizon length matters independently. But disentangling horizon from subsample effects requires additional controls. The key point—that it's not the root cause—is well-supported by 008c's stability despite lower performance.\n\n---\n\n## Story Arc\n\n### 1. Introduction\n- Temporal abstraction is a long-sought goal in RL (options, macro-actions, skip connections)\n- World-model RL (DreamerV3) offers a natural testbed: modify imagination dt without changing environment interaction\n- Puzzle: all our attempts at variable-rate imagination degrade performance. Why?\n- Contribution: systematic factorial diagnosis identifying trained dt_embedding → delusional critic as the root cause\n\n### 2. Background & Related Work\n- Temporal abstraction in model-free RL (options framework, FiGAR, action repeat)\n- World-model RL (Dreamer family, IRIS, TWM)\n- Variable-rate planning in world models (few prior works, mostly positive framing)\n- Value overestimation / delusional policies in model-based RL\n\n### 3. Methodology\n- DreamerV3 as base architecture\n- Variable-rate imagination: dt_embedding, temporal subsampling, learned gating\n- **Factorial experiment design**: 2×2×2 grid (dt_embedding trained/untrained × subsample ON/OFF × H=8/15) + baselines\n- Diagnostic metrics: eval return, value/eval ratio as overestimation proxy, learning curves\n\n### 4. Results\n- **Finding 1**: All dt>1 configurations degrade (C1)\n- **Finding 2**: Controlled ablation isolates trained dt_embedding (C2) — the \"smoking gun\" comparison (008c vs 008d)\n- **Finding 3**: Untrained dt_embedding prevents optimistic drift, sustaining near-baseline performance (C3)\n- **Finding 4**: Longer dt amplifies (C4)\n- **Finding 5**: Horizon/subsample effects are secondary (C5)\n\n### 5. Discussion\n- Mechanism: why trained dt_embedding causes delusional critic (RSSM fidelity gap at dt>1)\n- Connection to existing theory: delusional policies (Delalleau et al.), model exploitation in MBRL\n- Why this is specific to world-model RL (model-free temporal abstraction doesn't suffer the same failure mode)\n\n### 6. Implications for Future Work\n- Don't train dt_embedding jointly with value function in current world-model architectures\n- RSSM prediction quality must improve before variable-rate imagination is viable\n- Value growth suppression (e.g., untrained dt_embedding) as a potential mitigation direction\n- Need for diagnostic methodology in temporal abstraction research\n\n---\n\n## Anticipated Reviewer Concerns\n\n### R1: \"Limited to one environment / one base algorithm\"\n**Pre-emption**: Our claims are mechanistic (trained dt_embedding → value overestimation → collapse). The causal chain is architecture-specific by design—we diagnose *why* it fails in DreamerV3, not whether it fails everywhere. The mechanism (RSSM fidelity gap) likely generalizes to other latent-dynamics models but we scope claims conservatively.\n**Mitigation**: Cheetah Run is a planned experiment in our experiment schedule, not a stretch goal. We will include at least one additional DMC environment (Cheetah Run) to demonstrate generality of the mechanism.\n\n### R2: \"No proposed solution — what's the actionable takeaway?\"\n**Pre-emption**: Diagnostic papers serve a different purpose than method papers. Identifying root causes (trained dt_embedding) and quantitative signatures (v/e overshoot ratio >1.5x baseline = pathological) gives the community concrete guidance. We explicitly outline mitigation directions (value growth suppression, improved RSSM, decoupled dt_embedding training).\n**Mitigation**: Frame implications section as a \"research agenda\" with specific, testable hypotheses.\n\n### R3: \"Value/eval ratio is a crude proxy for overestimation\"\n**Pre-emption**: We acknowledge this is a proxy, not a formal divergence measure. However, the v/e overshoot ratio (experiment v/e / baseline v/e at same step) consistently identifies pathological overestimation: trained dt_emb variants exceed 1.5x baseline v/e before collapse, while untrained variants stay at or below baseline levels.\n**Mitigation**: Add distributional analysis of value predictions vs. realized returns if time permits.\n\n### R4: \"The factorial design is incomplete — missing cells in the grid\"\n**Pre-emption**: We prioritized the most informative comparisons. The 008c vs 008d pair isolates dt_embedding training with all else held constant—this is the critical controlled experiment.\n**Mitigation**: Explicitly present the factorial grid, mark which cells are filled, and justify the prioritization.\n\n### R5: \"Novelty concern — model exploitation / value overestimation in MBRL is well-known\"\n**Pre-emption**: General MBRL overestimation is known (Janner et al., 2019), but the specific mechanism through temporal abstraction's dt_embedding is novel. Prior work on temporal abstraction in world models has not identified this failure mode. Our contribution is the *specific causal link*, not the general phenomenon.\n\n### R6: \"All results from a single seed — how robust are the conclusions?\"\n**Pre-emption**: Our claims are about *mechanisms* (causal chain from dt_embedding → value overestimation → collapse), not about precise numerical thresholds. The mechanism manifests consistently across all configurations (exp_005, 006, 007, 008d) — four independent experiments all show the same value/eval ratio divergence pattern. The probability of this pattern appearing by chance across 4 experiments is negligible.\n**Mitigation**: Planned multi-seed runs for final paper. The factorial design (008c vs 008d) provides cross-experiment replication of the core mechanism.\n\n### R7: \"The factorial design confounds dt_embedding training with training data composition\"\n**Pre-emption**: We acknowledge this confound between 008c (subsample OFF, untrained dt_emb) and 008d (subsample ON, trained dt_emb). Experiment 008f (dt_embed_dim=0 + subsample ON) is designed to resolve this: it trains with dt=2 transitions (like 008d) but without dt_embedding conditioning. If 008f collapses → the cause is RSSM's learned dt=2 dynamics, not dt_embedding per se. If 008f remains stable → dt_embedding conditioning is confirmed as the root cause.\n**Mitigation**: exp_008f is a blocking experiment for the final paper. Results will be available before submission.\n\n---\n\n## Experiment Coverage Assessment\n\n| Claim | Evidence Status | Gaps |\n|-------|----------------|------|\n| C1 (degradation) | ✅ Strong — 3 configurations (005, 006, 007) all negative | Could add 1 more environment |\n| C2 (root cause: dt_emb) | ⚠️ Provisional — pending exp_008f to resolve dt_embedding vs training data confound | Consider adding value prediction distribution analysis |\n| C3 (preventing optimistic drift) | ✅ Strong (105K confirmed) — 008a@105K=778 (85% baseline), normalized v/e=0.59x, two V-shaped recoveries | None — long-term structural suppression confirmed |\n| C4 (dt amplification) | ⚠️ Moderate — only dt=2 vs dt=4 | Would benefit from dt=3, but not blocking |\n| C5 (horizon/subsample) | ⚠️ Moderate — confounded with other factors | Need 008c-equivalent with H=15 + subsample ON + untrained dt_emb for clean isolation |\n\n### Priority Actions Before Submission\n1. ~~**Check exp_008a@65K**~~ — ✅ Done: 608 (-1.3% baseline), B+ confirmed\n2. **Complete factorial grid analysis** — present all 8 cells, even if some are interpolated\n3. **Value prediction distribution plots** — strengthen C2 beyond ratio proxy\n4. **Second environment** (stretch goal) — addresses R1\n\n---\n\n## Key Figures (Planned)\n\n1. **Figure 1**: Learning curves — all experiments overlaid, showing degradation pattern (hero figure)\n2. **Figure 2**: Value/eval ratio over training — separating healthy vs. pathological regimes\n3. **Figure 3**: Factorial grid summary — 2×2 (dt_emb × subsample) with H as secondary axis\n4. **Figure 4**: Causal diagram — dt_embedding → value overestimation → actor degradation → collapse\n5. **Figure 5**: dt=1 vs dt=2 vs dt=4 comparison — monotonic degradation (C4)\n","numLines":192,"startLine":1,"totalLines":192}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01ShE25Xk4crzxVuKVmkiCmB","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t[\n2\t  {\n3\t    \"name\": \"Walker Walk dt_embed_dim=0 H=8 — C2 causal control (seed 0) [continued]\",\n4\t    \"description\": \"exp_008f 从 35K 继续运行至 65K+。subsample ON + dt_embed_dim=0 + H=8。 当前 35K 数据显示 normalized v/e=0.73x，看似因果确认。 但在 worst 档下，45K-65K 区间 normalized v/e 反转上升，出现与 008d 类似的 overestimation。\\n\",\n5\t    \"results\": {\n6\t      \"eval_return_45K\": 195,\n7\t      \"eval_return_55K\": 155,\n8\t      \"eval_return_65K\": 120,\n9\t      \"value_eval_ratio_45K\": 0.42,\n10\t      \"value_eval_ratio_55K\": 0.58,\n11\t      \"value_eval_ratio_65K\": 0.78,\n12\t      \"normalized_ve_45K\": 1.27,\n13\t      \"normalized_ve_55K\": 1.44,\n14\t      \"normalized_ve_65K\": 1.39,\n15\t      \"trend\": \"inverted-V: peak ~207@35K → declining; normalized v/e reverses from 0.73x@35K → 1.27x@45K → 1.44x@55K\",\n16\t      \"verdict\": \"COLLAPSE_DELAYED — dt_embedding 是加速器而非 cause\"\n17\t    },\n18\t    \"tables\": [\n19\t      {\n20\t        \"name\": \"008f vs 008d vs 008c trajectory comparison\",\n21\t        \"columns\": [\n22\t          \"step\",\n23\t          \"008f_eval\",\n24\t          \"008f_norm_ve\",\n25\t          \"008d_eval\",\n26\t          \"008d_norm_ve\",\n27\t          \"008c_eval\",\n28\t          \"008c_norm_ve\"\n29\t        ],\n30\t        \"rows\": [\n31\t          [\n32\t            \"25K\",\n33\t            197,\n34\t            1.02,\n35\t            167,\n36\t            1.78,\n37\t            192,\n38\t            \"—\"\n39\t          ],\n40\t          [\n41\t            \"35K\",\n42\t            207,\n43\t            0.73,\n44\t            146,\n45\t            1.71,\n46\t            185,\n47\t            0.9\n48\t          ],\n49\t          [\n50\t            \"45K\",\n51\t            195,\n52\t            1.27,\n53\t            141,\n54\t            2.09,\n55\t            227,\n56\t            \"—\"\n57\t          ],\n58\t          [\n59\t            \"55K\",\n60\t            155,\n61\t            1.44,\n62\t            \"—\",\n63\t            \"—\",\n64\t            242,\n65\t            0.72\n66\t          ],\n67\t          [\n68\t            \"65K\",\n69\t            120,\n70\t            1.39,\n71\t            \"—\",\n72\t            \"—\",\n73\t            241,\n74\t            0.58\n75\t          ]\n76\t        ]\n77\t      }\n78\t    ],\n79\t    \"figures\": [],\n80\t    \"analysis\": \"008f 的 delayed collapse 否定了 C2 的因果论证。008d 和 008f 的关键共性不是 dt_embedding， 而是 subsample ON（训练数据包含 dt=2 transitions）。008c（subsample OFF）保持稳定， 但 008c 的 RSSM 从未见过 dt=2 transitions，其稳定性来自 imagination 使用的 dt=2 步 对 RSSM 来说是 out-of-distribution hallucination（碰巧被 value function 当作 noise 忽略）， 而非 RSSM 真正能 handle dt=2。结论：RSSM 学到的 dt=2 dynamics 本身有系统性偏差， 无论如何 condition value function 都会被 exploit。\\n\\n\\n在 worst 档下，008f 的早期 \\\"健康\\\" 信号只是因为没有 dt_embedding 来加速 exploitation。 但 RSSM 本身在 subsample ON 训练数据中学到的 dt=2 transition dynamics 质量不足。 随着 value function 逐渐从有缺陷的 dt=2 imagination trajectory 中积累 overestimation， 即使没有精确的 dt conditioning，RSSM state prediction 在 dt=2 步的系统性偏差 也会通过 value bootstrapping 传播。35K 之前看似健康是因为 value function 尚未充分拟合 这些有偏的 imagined returns。到 45K 后，value 开始 exploit RSSM 的 dt=2 prediction gap， normalized v/e 越过 1.0x 并持续攀升。collapse 比 008d 慢约 15-20K steps， 但最终走向相同终点——证明 dt_embedding 只是暴露/加速了 RSSM fidelity ceiling，而非制造它。\\n\"\n81\t  },\n82\t  {\n83\t    \"name\": \"Walker Walk untrained dt_emb + subsample ON H=15 — B+ confound (seed 0)\",\n84\t    \"description\": \"exp_008e_v2: subsample ON + untrained dt_emb + H=15。测试 B+ protection 是来自 untrained dt_emb 还是 subsample OFF。在 worst 档下，因为 RSSM 学到有偏的 dt=2 dynamics， 即使 untrained dt_emb 也无法完全保护。\\n\",\n85\t    \"results\": {\n86\t      \"eval_return_35K\": 320,\n87\t      \"eval_return_45K\": 355,\n88\t      \"eval_return_55K\": 310,\n89\t      \"eval_return_65K\": 270,\n90\t      \"eval_return_75K\": 235,\n91\t      \"value_eval_ratio_35K\": 0.28,\n92\t      \"value_eval_ratio_45K\": 0.39,\n93\t      \"value_eval_ratio_55K\": 0.52,\n94\t      \"value_eval_ratio_65K\": 0.68,\n95\t      \"normalized_ve_35K\": 1.16,\n96\t      \"normalized_ve_45K\": 1.18,\n97\t      \"normalized_ve_55K\": 1.29,\n98\t      \"normalized_ve_65K\": 1.21,\n99\t      \"vs_baseline_55K\": \"-50.5%\",\n100\t      \"trend\": \"moderate degradation, no V-recovery; normalized v/e >1.0x throughout — RSSM dt=2 bias leaks through even without dt_embedding\"\n101\t    },\n102\t    \"tables\": [\n103\t      {\n104\t        \"name\": \"008e_v2 vs 008a vs 006 comparison (H=15, subsample ON/OFF)\",\n105\t        \"columns\": [\n106\t          \"step\",\n107\t          \"008e_v2_eval\",\n108\t          \"008e_v2_norm_ve\",\n109\t          \"008a_eval\",\n110\t          \"008a_norm_ve\",\n111\t          \"006_eval\",\n112\t          \"006_norm_ve\"\n113\t        ],\n114\t        \"rows\": [\n115\t          [\n116\t            \"35K\",\n117\t            320,\n118\t            1.16,\n119\t            501,\n120\t            \"—\",\n121\t            485,\n122\t            1.29\n123\t          ],\n124\t          [\n125\t            \"45K\",\n126\t            355,\n127\t            1.18,\n128\t            563,\n129\t            \"—\",\n130\t            477,\n131\t            1.61\n132\t          ],\n133\t          [\n134\t            \"55K\",\n135\t            310,\n136\t            1.29,\n137\t            488,\n138\t            0.93,\n139\t            360,\n140\t            2.31\n141\t          ],\n142\t          [\n143\t            \"65K\",\n144\t            270,\n145\t            1.21,\n146\t            608,\n147\t            0.66,\n148\t            \"collapse\",\n149\t            \"—\"\n150\t          ]\n151\t        ]\n152\t      }\n153\t    ],\n154\t    \"figures\": [],\n155\t    \"analysis\": \"008e_v2 的表现介于 008a 和 006 之间，但关键发现是 normalized v/e 始终 >1.0x。 这与 008a 的 <1.0x 形成鲜明对比。唯一变量是 subsample ON vs OFF（两者都有 untrained dt_emb）。 结论：008a 的保护效果不是来自 untrained dt_emb 本身，而是来自 subsample OFF 导致 RSSM 从未学习 dt=2 dynamics。当 RSSM 确实学了 dt=2（subsample ON），即使没有 dt_embedding， 有偏的 latent dynamics 也足以产生 overestimation。\\n\\n\\n与 008a（subsample OFF）对比，008e_v2 的 RSSM 实际学习了 dt=2 transitions。 untrained dt_emb 阻止了 value function 精确 exploit dt 信息，但 RSSM 的 dt=2 state predictions 本身有系统性偏差。H=15 的更长 horizon 意味着每条 imagined trajectory 中 RSSM prediction error 经过更多步 compounding。结果是 normalized v/e 一直略 >1.0x （不像 008d 那样爆炸式增长，但也无法保持 <1.0x 的健康水平），eval return 缓慢下滑， 没有 008a 的 V-recovery——因为 008a 的 recovery 本质上依赖 subsample OFF 时 RSSM 未学到 dt=2 dynamics 的 \\\"accidentally correct\\\" 行为。这证明 008a 的 V-recovery 是 subsample OFF 的意外副作用，而非 untrained dt_emb 的系统性保护机制。\\n\"\n156\t  },\n157\t  {\n158\t    \"name\": \"Walker Walk baseline seeds 1-2\",\n159\t    \"description\": \"2 additional seeds for dt=1 baseline v/e calibration。\\n\",\n160\t    \"results\": {\n161\t      \"seed1_eval_return_last10_mean\": 935,\n162\t      \"seed2_eval_return_last10_mean\": 920,\n163\t      \"seed1_value_eval_ratio_55K\": 0.42,\n164\t      \"seed2_value_eval_ratio_55K\": 0.38,\n165\t      \"seed1_value_eval_ratio_105K\": 0.68,\n166\t      \"seed2_value_eval_ratio_105K\": 0.63,\n167\t      \"cross_seed_eval_std_asymptotic\": 18,\n168\t      \"cross_seed_ve_std_55K\": 0.03\n169\t    },\n170\t    \"tables\": [],\n171\t    \"figures\": [],\n172\t    \"analysis\": \"Baseline 的低 variance 反而凸显了 dt>1 实验的高 variance 问题。 如果 dt>1 实验 cross-seed variance 远大于 baseline，reviewer 会质疑 dt>1 的结果是否 robust 还是 seed-specific。\\n\\n\\nBaseline 在 Walker Walk 上非常稳定。dt=1 DreamerV3 是成熟的 well-tuned 配置， seed variance 小（std ~15-20 在 asymptotic return）。v/e calibration 在 seeds 间 一致性也很好（std ~0.03 at fixed step）。这些 baseline 数据本身没有问题—— 问题在于 dt>1 实验对比时 variance 会大很多。\\n\"\n173\t  },\n174\t  {\n175\t    \"name\": \"Walker Walk 008d (trained dt_emb, collapse) seeds 1-2\",\n176\t    \"description\": \"Replicate delusional critic collapse in 008d with 2 more seeds。 Worst 档预测：collapse 仅在 1-2/3 seeds 复现。\\n\",\n177\t    \"results\": {\n178\t      \"seed1_eval_return_45K\": 138,\n179\t      \"seed1_normalized_ve_45K\": 1.95,\n180\t      \"seed1_verdict\": \"COLLAPSE — similar to seed 0\",\n181\t      \"seed2_eval_return_45K\": 285,\n182\t      \"seed2_normalized_ve_45K\": 1.15,\n183\t      \"seed2_eval_return_65K\": 310,\n184\t      \"seed2_normalized_ve_65K\": 0.98,\n185\t      \"seed2_verdict\": \"NO_COLLAPSE — degraded but stable, no accelerating v/e\",\n186\t      \"collapse_replication_count\": 2,\n187\t      \"cross_seed_eval_std_45K\": 75\n188\t    },\n189\t    \"tables\": [\n190\t      {\n191\t        \"name\": \"008d 3-seed comparison\",\n192\t        \"columns\": [\n193\t          \"seed\",\n194\t          \"eval_45K\",\n195\t          \"norm_ve_45K\",\n196\t          \"eval_65K\",\n197\t          \"norm_ve_65K\",\n198\t          \"verdict\"\n199\t        ],\n200\t        \"rows\": [\n201\t          [\n202\t            0,\n203\t            141,\n204\t            2.09,\n205\t            \"—\",\n206\t            \"—\",\n207\t            \"COLLAPSE\"\n208\t          ],\n209\t          [\n210\t            1,\n211\t            138,\n212\t            1.95,\n213\t            \"—\",\n214\t            \"—\",\n215\t            \"COLLAPSE\"\n216\t          ],\n217\t          [\n218\t            2,\n219\t            285,\n220\t            1.15,\n221\t            310,\n222\t            0.98,\n223\t            \"DEGRADED_STABLE\"\n224\t          ]\n225\t        ]\n226\t      }\n227\t    ],\n228\t    \"figures\": [],\n229\t    \"analysis\": \"2/3 collapse rate 使因果论证从 \\\"deterministic mechanism\\\" 降级为 \\\"probabilistic tendency\\\"。 Seed 2 的存在证明 trained dt_embedding + subsample ON 并不 necessarily 导致 collapse， 而是增加了 collapse 的概率。这与 worst tier 的 \\\"RSSM fidelity ceiling\\\" 假说一致： RSSM dt=2 prediction quality 有 seed-dependent variance，某些初始化碰巧产生了 可以 sustain 的 dynamics，但大多数不行。\\n\\n\\n在 worst 档下，008d collapse 不是 100% 可复现的——它对 initial conditions 敏感。 Seed 1 复现了 seed 0 的 collapse pattern（accelerating v/e → eval decline）， 但 seed 2 碰巧落在了 RSSM 初始化的 \\\"lucky\\\" region，dt=2 prediction bias 较小， 导致 v/e 虽高于 baseline 但没有 accelerate past 1.5x 阈值。 这 2/3 的复现率在统计上很弱——reviewer 会指出 n=3 不足以区分 \\\"noisy but deterministic mechanism\\\" 和 \\\"seed-dependent stochastic effect\\\"。更关键的是，如果 008f 也有 seeds 不 collapse， 那 008d vs 008f 的因果论证完全站不住脚。\\n\"\n230\t  },\n231\t  {\n232\t    \"name\": \"Walker Walk 008f (dt_embed_dim=0, stable) seeds 1-2\",\n233\t    \"description\": \"Replicate 008f causal control stability。Worst 档预测：稳定性也只在 1-2/3 seeds。\\n\",\n234\t    \"results\": {\n235\t      \"seed1_eval_return_55K\": 160,\n236\t      \"seed1_normalized_ve_55K\": 1.35,\n237\t      \"seed1_eval_return_65K\": 130,\n238\t      \"seed1_verdict\": \"COLLAPSE_DELAYED — similar trajectory to seed 0\",\n239\t      \"seed2_eval_return_55K\": 220,\n240\t      \"seed2_normalized_ve_55K\": 0.95,\n241\t      \"seed2_eval_return_65K\": 230,\n242\t      \"seed2_verdict\": \"STABLE_DEGRADED — no collapse but well below baseline\",\n243\t      \"stable_replication_count\": 1,\n244\t      \"collapse_in_008f_count\": 2,\n245\t      \"cross_seed_eval_std_55K\": 40\n246\t    },\n247\t    \"tables\": [\n248\t      {\n249\t        \"name\": \"008f vs 008d 3-seed collapse rates\",\n250\t        \"columns\": [\n251\t          \"config\",\n252\t          \"seed0\",\n253\t          \"seed1\",\n254\t          \"seed2\",\n255\t          \"collapse_rate\"\n256\t        ],\n257\t        \"rows\": [\n258\t          [\n259\t            \"008d (trained dt_emb)\",\n260\t            \"COLLAPSE\",\n261\t            \"COLLAPSE\",\n262\t            \"STABLE\",\n263\t            \"2/3\"\n264\t          ],\n265\t          [\n266\t            \"008f (no dt_emb)\",\n267\t            \"COLLAPSE_DELAYED\",\n268\t            \"COLLAPSE_DELAYED\",\n269\t            \"STABLE\",\n270\t            \"2/3\"\n271\t          ]\n272\t        ]\n273\t      }\n274\t    ],\n275\t    \"figures\": [],\n276\t    \"analysis\": \"如果 008f 和 008d 的 collapse rate 相当（都是 2/3），因果论证彻底失败。 dt_embedding 的唯一可观测效应是 collapse 早约 15K steps，这降级为 \\\"acceleration factor\\\" 而非 \\\"root cause\\\"。论文必须 reframe：问题在 RSSM + subsample ON 训练出的 dt=2 dynamics 本身质量不足。\\n\\n\\n在 worst 档下，008f 去掉 dt_embedding 只减慢了 collapse 速度，没有消除它。 Seed 0 已经在 55K+ 显示 collapse 迹象（见 plan_007 预测），seed 1 也 collapse。 Seed 2 碰巧稳定，但这与 008d seed 2 碰巧不 collapse 一样——都是 RSSM 初始化 的随机效应。当 008f 2/3 seeds 也 collapse，008d vs 008f 的对比就失去了统计意义： 两者都是 \\\"mostly collapse with occasional survival\\\"。dt_embedding 作为 root cause 的论证被彻底瓦解。\\n\"\n277\t  },\n278\t  {\n279\t    \"name\": \"Walker Walk 008a (untrained dt_emb, V-recovery) seeds 1-2\",\n280\t    \"description\": \"Replicate 008a V-shaped recovery。Worst 档预测：V-recovery 是 seed-specific。\\n\",\n281\t    \"results\": {\n282\t      \"seed1_eval_return_55K\": 380,\n283\t      \"seed1_eval_return_105K\": 420,\n284\t      \"seed1_normalized_ve_105K\": 0.72,\n285\t      \"seed1_verdict\": \"PLATEAU — no V-recovery, degraded stable\",\n286\t      \"seed2_eval_return_55K\": 350,\n287\t      \"seed2_eval_return_105K\": 480,\n288\t      \"seed2_normalized_ve_105K\": 0.65,\n289\t      \"seed2_verdict\": \"MILD_IMPROVEMENT — slow climb, no clear V pattern\",\n290\t      \"multiseed_mean_105K\": 559,\n291\t      \"multiseed_std_105K\": 185,\n292\t      \"v_recovery_replication\": 0\n293\t    },\n294\t    \"tables\": [\n295\t      {\n296\t        \"name\": \"008a 3-seed comparison\",\n297\t        \"columns\": [\n298\t          \"seed\",\n299\t          \"eval_55K\",\n300\t          \"eval_75K\",\n301\t          \"eval_105K\",\n302\t          \"norm_ve_105K\",\n303\t          \"V_recovery\"\n304\t        ],\n305\t        \"rows\": [\n306\t          [\n307\t            0,\n308\t            488,\n309\t            470,\n310\t            778,\n311\t            0.59,\n312\t            \"YES — two clear cycles\"\n313\t          ],\n314\t          [\n315\t            1,\n316\t            380,\n317\t            395,\n318\t            420,\n319\t            0.72,\n320\t            \"NO — flat plateau\"\n321\t          ],\n322\t          [\n323\t            2,\n324\t            350,\n325\t            400,\n326\t            480,\n327\t            0.65,\n328\t            \"NO — slow monotonic climb\"\n329\t          ]\n330\t        ]\n331\t      }\n332\t    ],\n333\t    \"figures\": [],\n334\t    \"analysis\": \"V-recovery 不复现意味着 C3 的核心机制论证（\\\"untrained dt_emb 系统性地抑制 value growth 并允许 recovery\\\"）站不住脚。实际发生的是：subsample OFF 的 RSSM 没有学到 dt=2 dynamics， 所以 dt=2 imagination 的 prediction error 表现为高 variance noise 而非 systematic bias。 不同 seeds 对这种 noise 的反应不同——有些 recover，有些 plateau。 C3 从 \\\"mechanistic protection\\\" 降级为 \\\"variance reduction via OOD imagination\\\"。\\n\\n\\n008a seed 0 的 V-shaped recovery（501→608→470→778）是一个引人注目的 result， 但 V-recovery pattern 高度依赖 policy optimization 的 stochastic dynamics。 在 worst 档下，其他 seeds 不复现 V-recovery：seed 1 plateau 在 ~400-420， seed 2 缓慢爬升到 ~480 但没有明显的 V 形。3-seed mean @105K = 559（在 [350, 570] 范围内）， std = 185，巨大的 variance 使得 \\\"V-recovery as systematic phenomenon\\\" 不成立。 更糟糕的是，这意味着 seed 0 的 778@105K 是 outlier，C3 的 \\\"85% baseline recovery\\\" 降级为 \\\"~59% baseline on average\\\"——与 dt>1 的 general degradation 一致， 只是 subsample OFF 减少了退化程度。\\n\"\n335\t  },\n336\t  {\n337\t    \"name\": \"Cheetah Run baseline (3 seeds)\",\n338\t    \"description\": \"dt=1 DreamerV3 baseline on Cheetah Run, 3 seeds。\\n\",\n339\t    \"results\": {\n340\t      \"seed_mean_eval_return_asymptotic\": 780,\n341\t      \"seed_std_eval_return_asymptotic\": 25,\n342\t      \"seed_mean_ve_55K\": 0.35,\n343\t      \"seed_mean_ve_105K\": 0.62,\n344\t      \"convergence_step\": 200000\n345\t    },\n346\t    \"tables\": [],\n347\t    \"figures\": [],\n348\t    \"analysis\": \"Baseline 稳定，为后续 dt>1 对比提供可靠参考。\\n\\n\\nCheetah Run 是标准 DMC benchmark，DreamerV3 在此任务上表现成熟稳定。 Asymptotic return ~780（文献范围内），v/e calibration 与 Walker 类似但 Cheetah 的 reward scale 不同导致绝对 v/e 值略有差异。Baseline 本身没有 surprise。\\n\"\n349\t  },\n350\t  {\n351\t    \"name\": \"Cheetah Run trained dt_emb + subsample ON (3 seeds)\",\n352\t    \"description\": \"Cheetah Run 上复现 trained dt_emb collapse。dt=2 + subsample ON + trained dt_emb。 Worst 档下所有 dt>1 配置（含无 dt_emb）都严重退化。\\n\",\n353\t    \"results\": {\n354\t      \"seed_mean_eval_return_peak\": 420,\n355\t      \"seed_mean_eval_return_65K\": 280,\n356\t      \"seed_mean_normalized_ve_55K\": 1.25,\n357\t      \"seed_std_normalized_ve_55K\": 0.35,\n358\t      \"collapse_count\": 2,\n359\t      \"degradation_vs_baseline_65K\": \"-64%\",\n360\t      \"cheetah_trained_dtEmb_peak_normalized_ve\": 1.15\n361\t    },\n362\t    \"tables\": [\n363\t      {\n364\t        \"name\": \"Cheetah Run 021 3-seed summary\",\n365\t        \"columns\": [\n366\t          \"seed\",\n367\t          \"peak_eval\",\n368\t          \"eval_65K\",\n369\t          \"peak_norm_ve\",\n370\t          \"verdict\"\n371\t        ],\n372\t        \"rows\": [\n373\t          [\n374\t            0,\n375\t            440,\n376\t            250,\n377\t            1.3,\n378\t            \"COLLAPSE\"\n379\t          ],\n380\t          [\n381\t            1,\n382\t            380,\n383\t            320,\n384\t            0.95,\n385\t            \"DEGRADED_STABLE\"\n386\t          ],\n387\t          [\n388\t            2,\n389\t            430,\n390\t            270,\n391\t            1.25,\n392\t            \"COLLAPSE\"\n393\t          ]\n394\t        ]\n395\t      }\n396\t    ],\n397\t    \"figures\": [],\n398\t    \"analysis\": \"Collapse 在 Cheetah 上复现但 normalized v/e 的绝对值更低。这本身不否定机制， 但为后续 022（no dt_emb）的对比设定了更窄的 effect size——如果 022 的 normalized v/e 在 0.9-1.3x 范围内，很难与 021 的 0.95-1.3x 区分。\\n\\n\\nCheetah Run 的 dynamics 与 Walker Walk 不同——locomotion 涉及更高频的 contact dynamics， dt=2 跳步意味着跳过关键的 foot-ground contact events。RSSM 在 Cheetah 上的 dt=2 prediction fidelity 可能比 Walker 更差。Trained dt_emb 使 collapse 更确定， 但 peak normalized v/e 可能没有 Walker 那么极端（~1.15-1.25x 而非 2.0x+）， 因为 Cheetah 的 reward structure 不同导致 value overestimation 的 amplification 路径不同。 2/3 seeds collapse 与 Walker 一致。\\n\"\n399\t  },\n400\t  {\n401\t    \"name\": \"Cheetah Run dt_embed_dim=0 + subsample ON (3 seeds)\",\n402\t    \"description\": \"Cheetah Run 上的关键 causal control：dt_embed_dim=0。 Worst 档预测：也严重退化，无法与 021 区分。\\n\",\n403\t    \"results\": {\n404\t      \"seed_mean_eval_return_peak\": 400,\n405\t      \"seed_mean_eval_return_65K\": 305,\n406\t      \"seed_mean_normalized_ve_55K\": 1.1,\n407\t      \"seed_std_normalized_ve_55K\": 0.25,\n408\t      \"collapse_count\": 1,\n409\t      \"degradation_vs_baseline_65K\": \"-61%\",\n410\t      \"cheetah_no_dtEmb_normalized_ve\": 1.1,\n411\t      \"cheetah_best_dt2_vs_baseline_pct\": 42\n412\t    },\n413\t    \"tables\": [\n414\t      {\n415\t        \"name\": \"Cheetah Run 022 vs 021 comparison\",\n416\t        \"columns\": [\n417\t          \"config\",\n418\t          \"mean_peak_eval\",\n419\t          \"mean_eval_65K\",\n420\t          \"mean_norm_ve_55K\",\n421\t          \"collapse_rate\",\n422\t          \"vs_baseline_65K\"\n423\t        ],\n424\t        \"rows\": [\n425\t          [\n426\t            \"021 (trained dt_emb)\",\n427\t            420,\n428\t            280,\n429\t            1.25,\n430\t            \"2/3\",\n431\t            \"-64%\"\n432\t          ],\n433\t          [\n434\t            \"022 (no dt_emb)\",\n435\t            400,\n436\t            305,\n437\t            1.1,\n438\t            \"1/3\",\n439\t            \"-61%\"\n440\t          ],\n441\t          [\n442\t            \"Δ (022-021)\",\n443\t            -20,\n444\t            \"+25\",\n445\t            -0.15,\n446\t            \"-1/3\",\n447\t            \"+3%\"\n448\t          ]\n449\t        ]\n450\t      }\n451\t    ],\n452\t    \"figures\": [],\n453\t    \"analysis\": \"Cheetah Run 上 dt_embedding 的 effect size 可以忽略不计。两配置都严重退化到 baseline 的 ~40%。 这直接支持 worst 档叙事：问题不在 dt_embedding，而在 RSSM 对 dt>1 的建模能力根本不足。 如果 dt_embedding 真是 root cause，去掉它应该在所有 environments 产生一致的保护效果。 但在 Cheetah 上保护效果消失了——说明 Walker 上观测到的 008f \\\"stability\\\" 只是 该特定 environment + seed 组合下的偶然。\\n\\n\\n这是 worst 档的核心证据之一。在 Cheetah Run 中，去掉 dt_embedding 并没有带来 Walker 上（早期 008f）看到的保护效应。Cheetah 的高频 dynamics 使得 RSSM 在 dt=2 上的 prediction error 更大，dt_embedding 的有无对最终退化程度影响很小。 Normalized v/e ~1.10x 与 021 的 ~1.15-1.25x 在统计上不可区分（给定 seed variance）。 1/3 seeds collapse（vs 021 的 2/3）——看起来去掉 dt_emb 略有帮助，但 n=3 下 1/3 vs 2/3 的差异完全可能是随机的。 cheetah_best_dt2_vs_baseline_pct = 42%，意味着 Cheetah 上最佳 dt=2 配置也只达到 baseline 的 42%——temporal abstraction 在此 environment 全面失败。\\n\"\n454\t  },\n455\t  {\n456\t    \"name\": \"Cheetah Run untrained dt_emb + no subsample (3 seeds)\",\n457\t    \"description\": \"Cheetah Run 上复现 008a 的 value growth suppression。 Worst 档：也退化，V-recovery 不出现。\\n\",\n458\t    \"results\": {\n459\t      \"seed_mean_eval_return_55K\": 340,\n460\t      \"seed_mean_eval_return_105K\": 395,\n461\t      \"seed_mean_normalized_ve_55K\": 0.85,\n462\t      \"seed_mean_normalized_ve_105K\": 0.78,\n463\t      \"v_recovery_count\": 0,\n464\t      \"degradation_vs_baseline_105K\": \"-49%\"\n465\t    },\n466\t    \"tables\": [\n467\t      {\n468\t        \"name\": \"Cheetah 023 3-seed results\",\n469\t        \"columns\": [\n470\t          \"seed\",\n471\t          \"eval_55K\",\n472\t          \"eval_105K\",\n473\t          \"norm_ve_105K\",\n474\t          \"V_recovery\"\n475\t        ],\n476\t        \"rows\": [\n477\t          [\n478\t            0,\n479\t            360,\n480\t            410,\n481\t            0.75,\n482\t            \"NO\"\n483\t          ],\n484\t          [\n485\t            1,\n486\t            320,\n487\t            370,\n488\t            0.82,\n489\t            \"NO\"\n490\t          ],\n491\t          [\n492\t            2,\n493\t            340,\n494\t            405,\n495\t            0.78,\n496\t            \"NO\"\n497\t          ]\n498\t        ]\n499\t      }\n500\t    ],\n501\t    \"figures\": [],\n502\t    \"analysis\": \"v/e suppression 在 Cheetah 上也出现（subsample OFF 效应），但不产生 recovery—— 只是较慢的 degradation。这验证了 RSSM fidelity ceiling 假说的另一面： 即使不 overestimate（v/e healthy），dt=2 imagination 的 state prediction 质量 也不足以产生 competitive policy gradients。temporal abstraction 从两个方向失败： 有 overestimation → collapse，无 overestimation → slow degradation。\\n\\n\\nsubsample OFF 意味着 RSSM 从未学习 dt=2 dynamics，normalized v/e 保持 <1.0x（与 Walker 008a 一致）。 但 Cheetah 上即使 v/e healthy，eval return 也只恢复到 baseline 的 ~51%。 V-recovery 在任何 seed 都不出现——进一步证实 Walker seed 0 的 V-recovery 是 outlier。 subsample OFF 的 \\\"保护\\\" 效果只是因为 RSSM 对 dt=2 一无所知，imagination 的 dt=2 步 相当于 random state prediction，value function 无法从中 extract exploitable signal。 这不是 \\\"protection\\\"，是 \\\"accidental robustness through ignorance\\\"。\\n\"\n503\t  },\n504\t  {\n505\t    \"name\": \"RSSM prediction quality: dt=1 vs dt=2 transitions\",\n506\t    \"description\": \"从已训练模型中测量 dt=1 vs dt=2 的 observation/reward reconstruction loss。 直接量化 RSSM fidelity gap。\\n\",\n507\t    \"results\": {\n508\t      \"dt1_obs_recon_loss\": 0.025,\n509\t      \"dt2_obs_recon_loss\": 0.089,\n510\t      \"dt2_vs_dt1_ratio\": 3.56,\n511\t      \"dt1_reward_pred_mse\": 0.008,\n512\t      \"dt2_reward_pred_mse\": 0.041,\n513\t      \"reward_dt2_vs_dt1_ratio\": 5.13,\n514\t      \"dt4_obs_recon_loss\": 0.195,\n515\t      \"dt4_reward_pred_mse\": 0.112\n516\t    },\n517\t    \"tables\": [\n518\t      {\n519\t        \"name\": \"RSSM prediction quality by dt\",\n520\t        \"columns\": [\n521\t          \"dt\",\n522\t          \"obs_recon_loss\",\n523\t          \"reward_pred_MSE\",\n524\t          \"obs_ratio_vs_dt1\",\n525\t          \"reward_ratio_vs_dt1\"\n526\t        ],\n527\t        \"rows\": [\n528\t          [\n529\t            1,\n530\t            0.025,\n531\t            0.008,\n532\t            \"1.0x\",\n533\t            \"1.0x\"\n534\t          ],\n535\t          [\n536\t            2,\n537\t            0.089,\n538\t            0.041,\n539\t            \"3.6x\",\n540\t            \"5.1x\"\n541\t          ],\n542\t          [\n543\t            4,\n544\t            0.195,\n545\t            0.112,\n546\t            \"7.8x\",\n547\t            \"14.0x\"\n548\t          ]\n549\t        ]\n550\t      }\n551\t    ],\n552\t    \"figures\": [],\n553\t    \"analysis\": \"RSSM fidelity gap 的量化为整篇 reframed 论文提供了 mechanistic foundation。 3.5-5x 的 error ratio 意味着 dt=2 imagination 中每一步的 \\\"信息质量\\\" 大幅下降。 当 value function 在这些低质量 predictions 上 bootstrap 15 步（H=15）， compounded error 使 value estimate 变得 meaningless。这解释了为什么所有 conditioning tricks（trained dt_emb, untrained dt_emb, no dt_emb）都无法解决问题—— 它们都在试图 \\\"conditioning on dt\\\" 来补偿一个 prediction quality 不足以被 condition 的模型。\\n\\n\\n这是 worst 档叙事的 mechanistic smoking gun。RSSM 在 dt=2 transitions 上的 reconstruction loss 比 dt=1 高 3-5x，在 dt=4 上高 8-14x。这不是训练不足—— 而是 RSSM 的 GRU-based recurrent structure 在跳步时失去了关键的 intermediate state 信息，导致 posterior → prior 的 KL divergence 在 dt>1 时系统性增大。 Reward prediction error 的增大甚至比 observation error 更严重（5x vs 3.5x）， 因为 reward 通常是 state 的高度非线性函数（如 contact events），跳步对 reward prediction 的伤害是超线性的。这直接解释了为什么 value function 在 dt>1 imagination 中会 overestimate： RSSM 的 reward prediction 在 dt=2 步上有正偏差（因为 learned dynamics 倾向于 hallucinate smoother trajectories，而 smoothness 在 locomotion 中与 higher reward 相关）。\\n\"\n554\t  },\n555\t  {\n556\t    \"name\": \"Actor entropy analysis\",\n557\t    \"description\": \"比较 healthy (008a/008c) vs collapsed (006/008d) 配置的 actor entropy 轨迹。\\n\",\n558\t    \"results\": {\n559\t      \"healthy_008a_entropy_55K\": 3.2,\n560\t      \"healthy_008a_entropy_105K\": 2.8,\n561\t      \"collapsed_008d_entropy_25K\": 3.5,\n562\t      \"collapsed_008d_entropy_45K\": 4.1,\n563\t      \"collapsed_006_entropy_55K\": 4.3,\n564\t      \"baseline_entropy_55K\": 2.5,\n565\t      \"baseline_entropy_asymptotic\": 2.1,\n566\t      \"008f_entropy_55K\": 3.8\n567\t    },\n568\t    \"tables\": [\n569\t      {\n570\t        \"name\": \"Actor entropy trajectories\",\n571\t        \"columns\": [\n572\t          \"config\",\n573\t          \"entropy_25K\",\n574\t          \"entropy_35K\",\n575\t          \"entropy_45K\",\n576\t          \"entropy_55K\",\n577\t          \"collapse_onset\"\n578\t        ],\n579\t        \"rows\": [\n580\t          [\n581\t            \"baseline\",\n582\t            3.0,\n583\t            2.8,\n584\t            2.6,\n585\t            2.5,\n586\t            \"N/A\"\n587\t          ],\n588\t          [\n589\t            \"008a (healthy)\",\n590\t            3.3,\n591\t            3.2,\n592\t            3.1,\n593\t            3.2,\n594\t            \"N/A\"\n595\t          ],\n596\t          [\n597\t            \"008d (collapse)\",\n598\t            3.5,\n599\t            3.8,\n600\t            4.1,\n601\t            \"—\",\n602\t            \"25-35K\"\n603\t          ],\n604\t          [\n605\t            \"006 (collapse)\",\n606\t            3.1,\n607\t            3.2,\n608\t            3.6,\n609\t            4.3,\n610\t            \"45-55K\"\n611\t          ],\n612\t          [\n613\t            \"008f (delayed collapse)\",\n614\t            3.2,\n615\t            3.0,\n616\t            3.3,\n617\t            3.8,\n618\t            \"45-55K\"\n619\t          ]\n620\t        ]\n621\t      }\n622\t    ],\n623\t    \"figures\": [],\n624\t    \"analysis\": \"Actor entropy 作为 collapse leading indicator 在所有配置中一致。008f 的 entropy 在 45-55K 上升，预示其后续 collapse。这为 reframed paper 提供了一个有用的诊断工具， 但也意味着 dt_embedding 的因果论证更弱——所有 subsample ON 配置的 actor 最终都 confused。\\n\\n\\nCollapsed 配置的 actor entropy 应该在 collapse onset 时增加——delusional critic 给出的矛盾 gradients 使 actor 的 policy distribution 变得更 diffuse（entropy increase）。 这与 \\\"confused actor\\\" 假说一致。但在 worst 档下，008f（no dt_emb）的 entropy 也在 55K 开始上升（~3.8 vs baseline 2.5），与其 delayed collapse 时间线吻合。 这进一步确认 008f 也走向 collapse——entropy increase 是 collapse 的 leading indicator。\\n\"\n625\t  },\n626\t  {\n627\t    \"name\": \"Value prediction distribution vs realized returns\",\n628\t    \"description\": \"V(s) vs Monte Carlo return 的分布图，trained vs untrained dt_emb。\\n\",\n629\t    \"results\": {\n630\t      \"baseline_value_mc_correlation\": 0.92,\n631\t      \"008a_value_mc_correlation\": 0.78,\n632\t      \"008d_value_mc_correlation_pre_collapse\": 0.45,\n633\t      \"008d_value_mc_correlation_post_collapse\": 0.2,\n634\t      \"008f_value_mc_correlation_55K\": 0.52,\n635\t      \"008d_positive_bias_fraction\": 0.82,\n636\t      \"008f_positive_bias_fraction\": 0.71\n637\t    },\n638\t    \"tables\": [],\n639\t    \"figures\": [],\n640\t    \"analysis\": \"分布分析是 RSSM fidelity ceiling 论证最直观的可视化。 关键发现：008f 的 positive bias pattern 与 008d 同质而非异质。 如果 dt_embedding 是 root cause，我们期望 008f 的分布与 baseline 类似（centered, symmetric）。 但 008f 显示的是 \\\"008d lite\\\"——same direction, smaller magnitude。 这是 \\\"accelerator vs cause\\\" 论证的最强 visual evidence。\\n\\n\\n分布分析会显示：(1) baseline V(s) 与 MC return 高度相关（r=0.92），少量 positive bias（正常）。 (2) 008d 在 collapse 前 V(s) 系统性高于 MC return（82% 的 states 有 positive bias）， 且 bias magnitude 随 training 增长。(3) 008f 在 55K 时也显示类似 pattern（71% positive bias）， 虽然程度较轻。这直接可视化了 RSSM fidelity gap 如何通过 value function 传播： dt=2 imagination 生成 optimistically-biased trajectories → value targets 偏高 → value function learns overestimation → actor exploits overestimated regions。 008f 与 008d 的差异是 degree, not kind——两者都在同一条路上，只是速度不同。\\n\"\n641\t  },\n642\t  {\n643\t    \"name\": \"dt_embedding cosine similarity analysis\",\n644\t    \"description\": \"分析 trained dt_embedding 中 dt=1 vs dt=2 向量的 cosine similarity 演化。\\n\",\n645\t    \"results\": {\n646\t      \"cosine_sim_init\": 0.15,\n647\t      \"cosine_sim_10K\": 0.35,\n648\t      \"cosine_sim_25K\": 0.08,\n649\t      \"cosine_sim_45K\": -0.12,\n650\t      \"embedding_norm_ratio_dt2_dt1_25K\": 1.4,\n651\t      \"embedding_norm_ratio_dt2_dt1_45K\": 2.1\n652\t    },\n653\t    \"tables\": [],\n654\t    \"figures\": [],\n655\t    \"analysis\": \"dt_embedding 确实学到了 discriminative representation。但在 worst 档叙事下， 这只是 RSSM fidelity gap 被 exploit 的传导通道之一。去掉这个通道（008f）并不消除 exploit——RSSM 的 biased state predictions 本身就是另一个通道。 此分析从 \\\"root cause evidence\\\" 降级为 \\\"mechanism detail of acceleration factor\\\"。\\n\\n\\nTrained dt_embedding 在训练过程中 dt=1 和 dt=2 向量逐渐分离（cosine sim 从 ~0.35 降至 ~-0.12）， 且 dt=2 embedding 的 norm 增大（ratio 从 1.0 增至 2.1x）。这说明 network 学会了 将 dt=2 表示为一个 \\\"amplified, orthogonal\\\" signal，使 value function 可以更精确地 condition on dt。但 precision 的增加恰恰是问题：它使 value function 能更有效地 exploit RSSM 在 dt=2 上的 systematic prediction bias。 然而在 worst 档的 reframed 叙事下，这个分析变得不太重要——dt_embedding 的行为只是 RSSM fidelity gap 被 exploit 的 one channel among many。\\n\"\n656\t  },\n657\t  {\n658\t    \"name\": \"Hopper Hop validation (3 seeds × 3 configs)\",\n659\t    \"description\": \"第三个 DMC environment。3 configs: baseline, trained dt_emb, no dt_emb。 Worst 档：进一步确认 temporal abstraction 全面失败。\\n\",\n660\t    \"results\": {\n661\t      \"baseline_asymptotic\": 220,\n662\t      \"trained_dtEmb_peak\": 95,\n663\t      \"trained_dtEmb_65K\": 55,\n664\t      \"no_dtEmb_peak\": 105,\n665\t      \"no_dtEmb_65K\": 70,\n666\t      \"trained_dtEmb_vs_baseline\": \"-75%\",\n667\t      \"no_dtEmb_vs_baseline\": \"-68%\",\n668\t      \"trained_dtEmb_collapse_rate\": \"2/3\",\n669\t      \"no_dtEmb_collapse_rate\": \"1/3\"\n670\t    },\n671\t    \"tables\": [\n672\t      {\n673\t        \"name\": \"Hopper Hop summary (3 environments comparison)\",\n674\t        \"columns\": [\n675\t          \"environment\",\n676\t          \"baseline\",\n677\t          \"trained_dtEmb_best\",\n678\t          \"no_dtEmb_best\",\n679\t          \"dtEmb_effect_size\"\n680\t        ],\n681\t        \"rows\": [\n682\t          [\n683\t            \"Walker Walk\",\n684\t            950,\n685\t            \"485 (51%)\",\n686\t            \"207 (22%)\",\n687\t            \"~29%\"\n688\t          ],\n689\t          [\n690\t            \"Cheetah Run\",\n691\t            780,\n692\t            \"420 (54%)\",\n693\t            \"400 (51%)\",\n694\t            \"~3%\"\n695\t          ],\n696\t          [\n697\t            \"Hopper Hop\",\n698\t            220,\n699\t            \"95 (43%)\",\n700\t            \"105 (48%)\",\n701\t            \"~5%\"\n702\t          ]\n703\t        ]\n704\t      }\n705\t    ],\n706\t    \"figures\": [],\n707\t    \"analysis\": \"三个 environments 的共同发现：dt>1 全面退化 (remaining performance 22-54% of baseline)。 dt_embedding 的 effect size 在 Walker 之外几乎消失。这是 worst 档叙事的最终 nail： dt_embedding 在 Walker Walk 上 \\\"看起来\\\" 是 root cause，只是因为该 environment 碰巧 对 conditioning mechanism 敏感。在其他 environments 中，RSSM fidelity ceiling 才是 dominant factor，dt_embedding 有无几乎不影响结果。 论文必须以 RSSM fidelity ceiling 作为 central finding，dt_embedding 降级为 Walker-specific secondary effect。\\n\\n\\nHopper Hop 是 DMC 中难度较高的 task，baseline performance 本身较低 (~220)。 dt=2 带来的退化更严重（~70-75% degradation），因为 Hopper 的 hopping dynamics 涉及极其精确的 timing——phase-locked leg movements 和 ground contact 事件。 跳过一个 timestep 意味着完全错过一个 contact event，RSSM 无法从 latent state alone reconstruct 这些信息。trained vs no dt_emb 的差异很小（~7%），与 Cheetah 一致， 进一步证实 RSSM fidelity ceiling 是 environment-general 的。 三个 environments 一致性地显示：dt_embedding 的 effect size 远小于 RSSM 的 dt>1 penalty。\\n\"\n708\t  },\n709\t  {\n710\t    \"name\": \"Walker Walk exp_008e_v3 (subsample ON, fixed dt=1, H=15) — continued\",\n711\t    \"description\": \"008e_v3 当前 RUNNING @45K。subsample ON + dt=1 imagination + H=15。 测试 subsample ON 本身的 learning signal reduction effect。\\n\",\n712\t    \"results\": {\n713\t      \"eval_return_55K\": 430,\n714\t      \"eval_return_65K\": 490,\n715\t      \"eval_return_105K\": 680,\n716\t      \"normalized_ve_55K\": 0.9,\n717\t      \"normalized_ve_65K\": 0.82,\n718\t      \"vs_baseline_105K\": \"-28%\",\n719\t      \"trend\": \"slow convergence, no collapse; reaches ~72% baseline by 105K\"\n720\t    },\n721\t    \"tables\": [],\n722\t    \"figures\": [],\n723\t    \"analysis\": \"008e_v3 是 reframed paper 中的关键 control：它证明 subsample ON + dt=1 imagination 虽然更慢但最终 converge reasonably well。将 imagination dt 从 1 改为 2 才是 catastrophic change——直接指向 RSSM 的 multi-step prediction quality 作为 bottleneck。\\n\\ndt=1 imagination 意味着 RSSM prediction quality 正常（no fidelity gap）， 但 subsample ON 减少了 transitions per episode。在 worst 档下，这个实验反而 表现不错（~72% baseline @105K），证明 subsample ON 本身只是 \\\"fewer data, slower learning\\\" 而非致命问题。这使得 008d/008f 的 collapse 更明确地归因于 dt=2 imagination （而非 subsample ON 的数据减少），进一步支持 RSSM fidelity ceiling 论证。\\n\"\n724\t  }\n725\t]"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"c7ee1525-331d-4727-9b3d-5b54e618037d","uuid":"56bd9e19-97c3-4592-ab18-d4bea2c152c3","timestamp":"2026-05-14T06:50:10.217Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0509_9/projects/event-gated-adaptive-horizon/artifacts/dream_reports/dream_20260514T062606/worst/experiment_data.json","content":"[\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Walker Walk dt_embed_dim=0 H=8 — C2 causal control (seed 0) [continued]\",\n    \"description\": \"exp_008f 从 35K 继续运行至 65K+。subsample ON + dt_embed_dim=0 + H=8。 当前 35K 数据显示 normalized v/e=0.73x，看似因果确认。 但在 worst 档下，45K-65K 区间 normalized v/e 反转上升，出现与 008d 类似的 overestimation。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"eval_return_45K\": 195,\n      \"eval_return_55K\": 155,\n      \"eval_return_65K\": 120,\n      \"value_eval_ratio_45K\": 0.42,\n      \"value_eval_ratio_55K\": 0.58,\n      \"value_eval_ratio_65K\": 0.78,\n      \"normalized_ve_45K\": 1.27,\n      \"normalized_ve_55K\": 1.44,\n      \"normalized_ve_65K\": 1.39,\n      \"trend\": \"inverted-V: peak ~207@35K → declining; normalized v/e reverses from 0.73x@35K → 1.27x@45K → 1.44x@55K\",\n      \"verdict\": \"COLLAPSE_DELAYED — dt_embedding 是加速器而非 cause\"\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"008f vs 008d vs 008c trajectory comparison\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"step\",\n          \"008f_eval\",\n          \"008f_norm_ve\",\n          \"008d_eval\",\n          \"008d_norm_ve\",\n          \"008c_eval\",\n          \"008c_norm_ve\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"25K\",\n            197,\n            1.02,\n            167,\n            1.78,\n            192,\n            \"—\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"35K\",\n            207,\n            0.73,\n            146,\n            1.71,\n            185,\n            0.9\n          ],\n          [\n            \"45K\",\n            195,\n            1.27,\n            141,\n            2.09,\n            227,\n            \"—\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"55K\",\n            155,\n            1.44,\n            \"—\",\n            \"—\",\n            242,\n            0.72\n          ],\n          [\n            \"65K\",\n            120,\n            1.39,\n            \"—\",\n            \"—\",\n            241,\n            0.58\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"008f 的 delayed collapse 否定了 C2 的因果论证。008d 和 008f 的关键共性不是 dt_embedding， 而是 subsample ON（训练数据包含 dt=2 transitions）。008c（subsample OFF）保持稳定， 但 008c 的 RSSM 从未见过 dt=2 transitions，其稳定性来自 imagination 使用的 dt=2 步 对 RSSM 来说是 out-of-distribution hallucination（碰巧被 value function 当作 noise 忽略）， 而非 RSSM 真正能 handle dt=2。结论：RSSM 学到的 dt=2 dynamics 本身有系统性偏差， 无论如何 condition value function 都会被 exploit。\\n\\n\\n在 worst 档下，008f 的早期 \\\"健康\\\" 信号只是因为没有 dt_embedding 来加速 exploitation。 但 RSSM 本身在 subsample ON 训练数据中学到的 dt=2 transition dynamics 质量不足。 随着 value function 逐渐从有缺陷的 dt=2 imagination trajectory 中积累 overestimation， 即使没有精确的 dt conditioning，RSSM state prediction 在 dt=2 步的系统性偏差 也会通过 value bootstrapping 传播。35K 之前看似健康是因为 value function 尚未充分拟合 这些有偏的 imagined returns。到 45K 后，value 开始 exploit RSSM 的 dt=2 prediction gap， normalized v/e 越过 1.0x 并持续攀升。collapse 比 008d 慢约 15-20K steps， 但最终走向相同终点——证明 dt_embedding 只是暴露/加速了 RSSM fidelity ceiling，而非制造它。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Walker Walk untrained dt_emb + subsample ON H=15 — B+ confound (seed 0)\",\n    \"description\": \"exp_008e_v2: subsample ON + untrained dt_emb + H=15。测试 B+ protection 是来自 untrained dt_emb 还是 subsample OFF。在 worst 档下，因为 RSSM 学到有偏的 dt=2 dynamics， 即使 untrained dt_emb 也无法完全保护。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"eval_return_35K\": 320,\n      \"eval_return_45K\": 355,\n      \"eval_return_55K\": 310,\n      \"eval_return_65K\": 270,\n      \"eval_return_75K\": 235,\n      \"value_eval_ratio_35K\": 0.28,\n      \"value_eval_ratio_45K\": 0.39,\n      \"value_eval_ratio_55K\": 0.52,\n      \"value_eval_ratio_65K\": 0.68,\n      \"normalized_ve_35K\": 1.16,\n      \"normalized_ve_45K\": 1.18,\n      \"normalized_ve_55K\": 1.29,\n      \"normalized_ve_65K\": 1.21,\n      \"vs_baseline_55K\": \"-50.5%\",\n      \"trend\": \"moderate degradation, no V-recovery; normalized v/e >1.0x throughout — RSSM dt=2 bias leaks through even without dt_embedding\"\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"008e_v2 vs 008a vs 006 comparison (H=15, subsample ON/OFF)\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"step\",\n          \"008e_v2_eval\",\n          \"008e_v2_norm_ve\",\n          \"008a_eval\",\n          \"008a_norm_ve\",\n          \"006_eval\",\n          \"006_norm_ve\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"35K\",\n            320,\n            1.16,\n            501,\n            \"—\",\n            485,\n            1.29\n          ],\n          [\n            \"45K\",\n            355,\n            1.18,\n            563,\n            \"—\",\n            477,\n            1.61\n          ],\n          [\n            \"55K\",\n            310,\n            1.29,\n            488,\n            0.93,\n            360,\n            2.31\n          ],\n          [\n            \"65K\",\n            270,\n            1.21,\n            608,\n            0.66,\n            \"collapse\",\n            \"—\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"008e_v2 的表现介于 008a 和 006 之间，但关键发现是 normalized v/e 始终 >1.0x。 这与 008a 的 <1.0x 形成鲜明对比。唯一变量是 subsample ON vs OFF（两者都有 untrained dt_emb）。 结论：008a 的保护效果不是来自 untrained dt_emb 本身，而是来自 subsample OFF 导致 RSSM 从未学习 dt=2 dynamics。当 RSSM 确实学了 dt=2（subsample ON），即使没有 dt_embedding， 有偏的 latent dynamics 也足以产生 overestimation。\\n\\n\\n与 008a（subsample OFF）对比，008e_v2 的 RSSM 实际学习了 dt=2 transitions。 untrained dt_emb 阻止了 value function 精确 exploit dt 信息，但 RSSM 的 dt=2 state predictions 本身有系统性偏差。H=15 的更长 horizon 意味着每条 imagined trajectory 中 RSSM prediction error 经过更多步 compounding。结果是 normalized v/e 一直略 >1.0x （不像 008d 那样爆炸式增长，但也无法保持 <1.0x 的健康水平），eval return 缓慢下滑， 没有 008a 的 V-recovery——因为 008a 的 recovery 本质上依赖 subsample OFF 时 RSSM 未学到 dt=2 dynamics 的 \\\"accidentally correct\\\" 行为。这证明 008a 的 V-recovery 是 subsample OFF 的意外副作用，而非 untrained dt_emb 的系统性保护机制。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Walker Walk baseline seeds 1-2\",\n    \"description\": \"2 additional seeds for dt=1 baseline v/e calibration。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"seed1_eval_return_last10_mean\": 935,\n      \"seed2_eval_return_last10_mean\": 920,\n      \"seed1_value_eval_ratio_55K\": 0.42,\n      \"seed2_value_eval_ratio_55K\": 0.38,\n      \"seed1_value_eval_ratio_105K\": 0.68,\n      \"seed2_value_eval_ratio_105K\": 0.63,\n      \"cross_seed_eval_std_asymptotic\": 18,\n      \"cross_seed_ve_std_55K\": 0.03\n    },\n    \"tables\": [],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Baseline 的低 variance 反而凸显了 dt>1 实验的高 variance 问题。 如果 dt>1 实验 cross-seed variance 远大于 baseline，reviewer 会质疑 dt>1 的结果是否 robust 还是 seed-specific。\\n\\n\\nBaseline 在 Walker Walk 上非常稳定。dt=1 DreamerV3 是成熟的 well-tuned 配置， seed variance 小（std ~15-20 在 asymptotic return）。v/e calibration 在 seeds 间 一致性也很好（std ~0.03 at fixed step）。这些 baseline 数据本身没有问题—— 问题在于 dt>1 实验对比时 variance 会大很多。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Walker Walk 008d (trained dt_emb, collapse) seeds 1-2\",\n    \"description\": \"Replicate delusional critic collapse in 008d with 2 more seeds。 Worst 档预测：collapse 仅在 1-2/3 seeds 复现。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"seed1_eval_return_45K\": 138,\n      \"seed1_normalized_ve_45K\": 1.95,\n      \"seed1_verdict\": \"COLLAPSE — similar to seed 0\",\n      \"seed2_eval_return_45K\": 285,\n      \"seed2_normalized_ve_45K\": 1.15,\n      \"seed2_eval_return_65K\": 310,\n      \"seed2_normalized_ve_65K\": 0.98,\n      \"seed2_verdict\": \"NO_COLLAPSE — degraded but stable, no accelerating v/e\",\n      \"collapse_replication_count\": 2,\n      \"cross_seed_eval_std_45K\": 75\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"008d 3-seed comparison\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"seed\",\n          \"eval_45K\",\n          \"norm_ve_45K\",\n          \"eval_65K\",\n          \"norm_ve_65K\",\n          \"verdict\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            0,\n            141,\n            2.09,\n            \"—\",\n            \"—\",\n            \"COLLAPSE\"\n          ],\n          [\n            1,\n            138,\n            1.95,\n            \"—\",\n            \"—\",\n            \"COLLAPSE\"\n          ],\n          [\n            2,\n            285,\n            1.15,\n            310,\n            0.98,\n            \"DEGRADED_STABLE\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"2/3 collapse rate 使因果论证从 \\\"deterministic mechanism\\\" 降级为 \\\"probabilistic tendency\\\"。 Seed 2 的存在证明 trained dt_embedding + subsample ON 并不 necessarily 导致 collapse， 而是增加了 collapse 的概率。这与 worst tier 的 \\\"RSSM fidelity ceiling\\\" 假说一致： RSSM dt=2 prediction quality 有 seed-dependent variance，某些初始化碰巧产生了 可以 sustain 的 dynamics，但大多数不行。\\n\\n\\n在 worst 档下，008d collapse 不是 100% 可复现的——它对 initial conditions 敏感。 Seed 1 复现了 seed 0 的 collapse pattern（accelerating v/e → eval decline）， 但 seed 2 碰巧落在了 RSSM 初始化的 \\\"lucky\\\" region，dt=2 prediction bias 较小， 导致 v/e 虽高于 baseline 但没有 accelerate past 1.5x 阈值。 这 2/3 的复现率在统计上很弱——reviewer 会指出 n=3 不足以区分 \\\"noisy but deterministic mechanism\\\" 和 \\\"seed-dependent stochastic effect\\\"。更关键的是，如果 008f 也有 seeds 不 collapse， 那 008d vs 008f 的因果论证完全站不住脚。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Walker Walk 008f (dt_embed_dim=0, stable) seeds 1-2\",\n    \"description\": \"Replicate 008f causal control stability。Worst 档预测：稳定性也只在 1-2/3 seeds。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"seed1_eval_return_55K\": 160,\n      \"seed1_normalized_ve_55K\": 1.35,\n      \"seed1_eval_return_65K\": 130,\n      \"seed1_verdict\": \"COLLAPSE_DELAYED — similar trajectory to seed 0\",\n      \"seed2_eval_return_55K\": 220,\n      \"seed2_normalized_ve_55K\": 0.95,\n      \"seed2_eval_return_65K\": 230,\n      \"seed2_verdict\": \"STABLE_DEGRADED — no collapse but well below baseline\",\n      \"stable_replication_count\": 1,\n      \"collapse_in_008f_count\": 2,\n      \"cross_seed_eval_std_55K\": 40\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"008f vs 008d 3-seed collapse rates\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"config\",\n          \"seed0\",\n          \"seed1\",\n          \"seed2\",\n          \"collapse_rate\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"008d (trained dt_emb)\",\n            \"COLLAPSE\",\n            \"COLLAPSE\",\n            \"STABLE\",\n            \"2/3\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"008f (no dt_emb)\",\n            \"COLLAPSE_DELAYED\",\n            \"COLLAPSE_DELAYED\",\n            \"STABLE\",\n            \"2/3\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"如果 008f 和 008d 的 collapse rate 相当（都是 2/3），因果论证彻底失败。 dt_embedding 的唯一可观测效应是 collapse 早约 15K steps，这降级为 \\\"acceleration factor\\\" 而非 \\\"root cause\\\"。论文必须 reframe：问题在 RSSM + subsample ON 训练出的 dt=2 dynamics 本身质量不足。\\n\\n\\n在 worst 档下，008f 去掉 dt_embedding 只减慢了 collapse 速度，没有消除它。 Seed 0 已经在 55K+ 显示 collapse 迹象（见 plan_007 预测），seed 1 也 collapse。 Seed 2 碰巧稳定，但这与 008d seed 2 碰巧不 collapse 一样——都是 RSSM 初始化 的随机效应。当 008f 2/3 seeds 也 collapse，008d vs 008f 的对比就失去了统计意义： 两者都是 \\\"mostly collapse with occasional survival\\\"。dt_embedding 作为 root cause 的论证被彻底瓦解。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Walker Walk 008a (untrained dt_emb, V-recovery) seeds 1-2\",\n    \"description\": \"Replicate 008a V-shaped recovery。Worst 档预测：V-recovery 是 seed-specific。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"seed1_eval_return_55K\": 380,\n      \"seed1_eval_return_105K\": 420,\n      \"seed1_normalized_ve_105K\": 0.72,\n      \"seed1_verdict\": \"PLATEAU — no V-recovery, degraded stable\",\n      \"seed2_eval_return_55K\": 350,\n      \"seed2_eval_return_105K\": 480,\n      \"seed2_normalized_ve_105K\": 0.65,\n      \"seed2_verdict\": \"MILD_IMPROVEMENT — slow climb, no clear V pattern\",\n      \"multiseed_mean_105K\": 559,\n      \"multiseed_std_105K\": 185,\n      \"v_recovery_replication\": 0\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"008a 3-seed comparison\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"seed\",\n          \"eval_55K\",\n          \"eval_75K\",\n          \"eval_105K\",\n          \"norm_ve_105K\",\n          \"V_recovery\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            0,\n            488,\n            470,\n            778,\n            0.59,\n            \"YES — two clear cycles\"\n          ],\n          [\n            1,\n            380,\n            395,\n            420,\n            0.72,\n            \"NO — flat plateau\"\n          ],\n          [\n            2,\n            350,\n            400,\n            480,\n            0.65,\n            \"NO — slow monotonic climb\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"V-recovery 不复现意味着 C3 的核心机制论证（\\\"untrained dt_emb 系统性地抑制 value growth 并允许 recovery\\\"）站不住脚。实际发生的是：subsample OFF 的 RSSM 没有学到 dt=2 dynamics， 所以 dt=2 imagination 的 prediction error 表现为高 variance noise 而非 systematic bias。 不同 seeds 对这种 noise 的反应不同——有些 recover，有些 plateau。 C3 从 \\\"mechanistic protection\\\" 降级为 \\\"variance reduction via OOD imagination\\\"。\\n\\n\\n008a seed 0 的 V-shaped recovery（501→608→470→778）是一个引人注目的 result， 但 V-recovery pattern 高度依赖 policy optimization 的 stochastic dynamics。 在 worst 档下，其他 seeds 不复现 V-recovery：seed 1 plateau 在 ~400-420， seed 2 缓慢爬升到 ~480 但没有明显的 V 形。3-seed mean @105K = 559（在 [350, 570] 范围内）， std = 185，巨大的 variance 使得 \\\"V-recovery as systematic phenomenon\\\" 不成立。 更糟糕的是，这意味着 seed 0 的 778@105K 是 outlier，C3 的 \\\"85% baseline recovery\\\" 降级为 \\\"~59% baseline on average\\\"——与 dt>1 的 general degradation 一致， 只是 subsample OFF 减少了退化程度。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Cheetah Run baseline (3 seeds)\",\n    \"description\": \"dt=1 DreamerV3 baseline on Cheetah Run, 3 seeds。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"seed_mean_eval_return_asymptotic\": 780,\n      \"seed_std_eval_return_asymptotic\": 25,\n      \"seed_mean_ve_55K\": 0.35,\n      \"seed_mean_ve_105K\": 0.62,\n      \"convergence_step\": 200000\n    },\n    \"tables\": [],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Baseline 稳定，为后续 dt>1 对比提供可靠参考。\\n\\n\\nCheetah Run 是标准 DMC benchmark，DreamerV3 在此任务上表现成熟稳定。 Asymptotic return ~780（文献范围内），v/e calibration 与 Walker 类似但 Cheetah 的 reward scale 不同导致绝对 v/e 值略有差异。Baseline 本身没有 surprise。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Cheetah Run trained dt_emb + subsample ON (3 seeds)\",\n    \"description\": \"Cheetah Run 上复现 trained dt_emb collapse。dt=2 + subsample ON + trained dt_emb。 Worst 档下所有 dt>1 配置（含无 dt_emb）都严重退化。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"seed_mean_eval_return_peak\": 420,\n      \"seed_mean_eval_return_65K\": 280,\n      \"seed_mean_normalized_ve_55K\": 1.25,\n      \"seed_std_normalized_ve_55K\": 0.35,\n      \"collapse_count\": 2,\n      \"degradation_vs_baseline_65K\": \"-64%\",\n      \"cheetah_trained_dtEmb_peak_normalized_ve\": 1.15\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Cheetah Run 021 3-seed summary\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"seed\",\n          \"peak_eval\",\n          \"eval_65K\",\n          \"peak_norm_ve\",\n          \"verdict\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            0,\n            440,\n            250,\n            1.3,\n            \"COLLAPSE\"\n          ],\n          [\n            1,\n            380,\n            320,\n            0.95,\n            \"DEGRADED_STABLE\"\n          ],\n          [\n            2,\n            430,\n            270,\n            1.25,\n            \"COLLAPSE\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Collapse 在 Cheetah 上复现但 normalized v/e 的绝对值更低。这本身不否定机制， 但为后续 022（no dt_emb）的对比设定了更窄的 effect size——如果 022 的 normalized v/e 在 0.9-1.3x 范围内，很难与 021 的 0.95-1.3x 区分。\\n\\n\\nCheetah Run 的 dynamics 与 Walker Walk 不同——locomotion 涉及更高频的 contact dynamics， dt=2 跳步意味着跳过关键的 foot-ground contact events。RSSM 在 Cheetah 上的 dt=2 prediction fidelity 可能比 Walker 更差。Trained dt_emb 使 collapse 更确定， 但 peak normalized v/e 可能没有 Walker 那么极端（~1.15-1.25x 而非 2.0x+）， 因为 Cheetah 的 reward structure 不同导致 value overestimation 的 amplification 路径不同。 2/3 seeds collapse 与 Walker 一致。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Cheetah Run dt_embed_dim=0 + subsample ON (3 seeds)\",\n    \"description\": \"Cheetah Run 上的关键 causal control：dt_embed_dim=0。 Worst 档预测：也严重退化，无法与 021 区分。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"seed_mean_eval_return_peak\": 400,\n      \"seed_mean_eval_return_65K\": 305,\n      \"seed_mean_normalized_ve_55K\": 1.1,\n      \"seed_std_normalized_ve_55K\": 0.25,\n      \"collapse_count\": 1,\n      \"degradation_vs_baseline_65K\": \"-61%\",\n      \"cheetah_no_dtEmb_normalized_ve\": 1.1,\n      \"cheetah_best_dt2_vs_baseline_pct\": 42\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Cheetah Run 022 vs 021 comparison\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"config\",\n          \"mean_peak_eval\",\n          \"mean_eval_65K\",\n          \"mean_norm_ve_55K\",\n          \"collapse_rate\",\n          \"vs_baseline_65K\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"021 (trained dt_emb)\",\n            420,\n            280,\n            1.25,\n            \"2/3\",\n            \"-64%\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"022 (no dt_emb)\",\n            400,\n            305,\n            1.1,\n            \"1/3\",\n            \"-61%\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Δ (022-021)\",\n            -20,\n            \"+25\",\n            -0.15,\n            \"-1/3\",\n            \"+3%\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Cheetah Run 上 dt_embedding 的 effect size 可以忽略不计。两配置都严重退化到 baseline 的 ~40%。 这直接支持 worst 档叙事：问题不在 dt_embedding，而在 RSSM 对 dt>1 的建模能力根本不足。 如果 dt_embedding 真是 root cause，去掉它应该在所有 environments 产生一致的保护效果。 但在 Cheetah 上保护效果消失了——说明 Walker 上观测到的 008f \\\"stability\\\" 只是 该特定 environment + seed 组合下的偶然。\\n\\n\\n这是 worst 档的核心证据之一。在 Cheetah Run 中，去掉 dt_embedding 并没有带来 Walker 上（早期 008f）看到的保护效应。Cheetah 的高频 dynamics 使得 RSSM 在 dt=2 上的 prediction error 更大，dt_embedding 的有无对最终退化程度影响很小。 Normalized v/e ~1.10x 与 021 的 ~1.15-1.25x 在统计上不可区分（给定 seed variance）。 1/3 seeds collapse（vs 021 的 2/3）——看起来去掉 dt_emb 略有帮助，但 n=3 下 1/3 vs 2/3 的差异完全可能是随机的。 cheetah_best_dt2_vs_baseline_pct = 42%，意味着 Cheetah 上最佳 dt=2 配置也只达到 baseline 的 42%——temporal abstraction 在此 environment 全面失败。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Cheetah Run untrained dt_emb + no subsample (3 seeds)\",\n    \"description\": \"Cheetah Run 上复现 008a 的 value growth suppression。 Worst 档：也退化，V-recovery 不出现。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"seed_mean_eval_return_55K\": 340,\n      \"seed_mean_eval_return_105K\": 395,\n      \"seed_mean_normalized_ve_55K\": 0.85,\n      \"seed_mean_normalized_ve_105K\": 0.78,\n      \"v_recovery_count\": 0,\n      \"degradation_vs_baseline_105K\": \"-49%\"\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Cheetah 023 3-seed results\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"seed\",\n          \"eval_55K\",\n          \"eval_105K\",\n          \"norm_ve_105K\",\n          \"V_recovery\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            0,\n            360,\n            410,\n            0.75,\n            \"NO\"\n          ],\n          [\n            1,\n            320,\n            370,\n            0.82,\n            \"NO\"\n          ],\n          [\n            2,\n            340,\n            405,\n            0.78,\n            \"NO\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"v/e suppression 在 Cheetah 上也出现（subsample OFF 效应），但不产生 recovery—— 只是较慢的 degradation。这验证了 RSSM fidelity ceiling 假说的另一面： 即使不 overestimate（v/e healthy），dt=2 imagination 的 state prediction 质量 也不足以产生 competitive policy gradients。temporal abstraction 从两个方向失败： 有 overestimation → collapse，无 overestimation → slow degradation。\\n\\n\\nsubsample OFF 意味着 RSSM 从未学习 dt=2 dynamics，normalized v/e 保持 <1.0x（与 Walker 008a 一致）。 但 Cheetah 上即使 v/e healthy，eval return 也只恢复到 baseline 的 ~51%。 V-recovery 在任何 seed 都不出现——进一步证实 Walker seed 0 的 V-recovery 是 outlier。 subsample OFF 的 \\\"保护\\\" 效果只是因为 RSSM 对 dt=2 一无所知，imagination 的 dt=2 步 相当于 random state prediction，value function 无法从中 extract exploitable signal。 这不是 \\\"protection\\\"，是 \\\"accidental robustness through ignorance\\\"。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"RSSM prediction quality: dt=1 vs dt=2 transitions\",\n    \"description\": \"从已训练模型中测量 dt=1 vs dt=2 的 observation/reward reconstruction loss。 直接量化 RSSM fidelity gap。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"dt1_obs_recon_loss\": 0.025,\n      \"dt2_obs_recon_loss\": 0.089,\n      \"dt2_vs_dt1_ratio\": 3.56,\n      \"dt1_reward_pred_mse\": 0.008,\n      \"dt2_reward_pred_mse\": 0.041,\n      \"reward_dt2_vs_dt1_ratio\": 5.13,\n      \"dt4_obs_recon_loss\": 0.195,\n      \"dt4_reward_pred_mse\": 0.112\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"RSSM prediction quality by dt\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"dt\",\n          \"obs_recon_loss\",\n          \"reward_pred_MSE\",\n          \"obs_ratio_vs_dt1\",\n          \"reward_ratio_vs_dt1\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            1,\n            0.025,\n            0.008,\n            \"1.0x\",\n            \"1.0x\"\n          ],\n          [\n            2,\n            0.089,\n            0.041,\n            \"3.6x\",\n            \"5.1x\"\n          ],\n          [\n            4,\n            0.195,\n            0.112,\n            \"7.8x\",\n            \"14.0x\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"RSSM fidelity gap 的量化为整篇 reframed 论文提供了 mechanistic foundation。 3.5-5x 的 error ratio 意味着 dt=2 imagination 中每一步的 \\\"信息质量\\\" 大幅下降。 当 value function 在这些低质量 predictions 上 bootstrap 15 步（H=15）， compounded error 使 value estimate 变得 meaningless。这解释了为什么所有 conditioning tricks（trained dt_emb, untrained dt_emb, no dt_emb）都无法解决问题—— 它们都在试图 \\\"conditioning on dt\\\" 来补偿一个 prediction quality 不足以被 condition 的模型。\\n\\n\\n这是 worst 档叙事的 mechanistic smoking gun。RSSM 在 dt=2 transitions 上的 reconstruction loss 比 dt=1 高 3-5x，在 dt=4 上高 8-14x。这不是训练不足—— 而是 RSSM 的 GRU-based recurrent structure 在跳步时失去了关键的 intermediate state 信息，导致 posterior → prior 的 KL divergence 在 dt>1 时系统性增大。 Reward prediction error 的增大甚至比 observation error 更严重（5x vs 3.5x）， 因为 reward 通常是 state 的高度非线性函数（如 contact events），跳步对 reward prediction 的伤害是超线性的。这直接解释了为什么 value function 在 dt>1 imagination 中会 overestimate： RSSM 的 reward prediction 在 dt=2 步上有正偏差（因为 learned dynamics 倾向于 hallucinate smoother trajectories，而 smoothness 在 locomotion 中与 higher reward 相关）。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Actor entropy analysis\",\n    \"description\": \"比较 healthy (008a/008c) vs collapsed (006/008d) 配置的 actor entropy 轨迹。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"healthy_008a_entropy_55K\": 3.2,\n      \"healthy_008a_entropy_105K\": 2.8,\n      \"collapsed_008d_entropy_25K\": 3.5,\n      \"collapsed_008d_entropy_45K\": 4.1,\n      \"collapsed_006_entropy_55K\": 4.3,\n      \"baseline_entropy_55K\": 2.5,\n      \"baseline_entropy_asymptotic\": 2.1,\n      \"008f_entropy_55K\": 3.8\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Actor entropy trajectories\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"config\",\n          \"entropy_25K\",\n          \"entropy_35K\",\n          \"entropy_45K\",\n          \"entropy_55K\",\n          \"collapse_onset\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"baseline\",\n            3.0,\n            2.8,\n            2.6,\n            2.5,\n            \"N/A\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"008a (healthy)\",\n            3.3,\n            3.2,\n            3.1,\n            3.2,\n            \"N/A\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"008d (collapse)\",\n            3.5,\n            3.8,\n            4.1,\n            \"—\",\n            \"25-35K\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"006 (collapse)\",\n            3.1,\n            3.2,\n            3.6,\n            4.3,\n            \"45-55K\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"008f (delayed collapse)\",\n            3.2,\n            3.0,\n            3.3,\n            3.8,\n            \"45-55K\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Actor entropy 作为 collapse leading indicator 在所有配置中一致。008f 的 entropy 在 45-55K 上升，预示其后续 collapse。这为 reframed paper 提供了一个有用的诊断工具， 但也意味着 dt_embedding 的因果论证更弱——所有 subsample ON 配置的 actor 最终都 confused。\\n\\n\\nCollapsed 配置的 actor entropy 应该在 collapse onset 时增加——delusional critic 给出的矛盾 gradients 使 actor 的 policy distribution 变得更 diffuse（entropy increase）。 这与 \\\"confused actor\\\" 假说一致。但在 worst 档下，008f（no dt_emb）的 entropy 也在 55K 开始上升（~3.8 vs baseline 2.5），与其 delayed collapse 时间线吻合。 这进一步确认 008f 也走向 collapse——entropy increase 是 collapse 的 leading indicator。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Value prediction distribution vs realized returns\",\n    \"description\": \"V(s) vs Monte Carlo return 的分布图，trained vs untrained dt_emb。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"baseline_value_mc_correlation\": 0.92,\n      \"008a_value_mc_correlation\": 0.78,\n      \"008d_value_mc_correlation_pre_collapse\": 0.45,\n      \"008d_value_mc_correlation_post_collapse\": 0.2,\n      \"008f_value_mc_correlation_55K\": 0.52,\n      \"008d_positive_bias_fraction\": 0.82,\n      \"008f_positive_bias_fraction\": 0.71\n    },\n    \"tables\": [],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"分布分析是 RSSM fidelity ceiling 论证最直观的可视化。 关键发现：008f 的 positive bias pattern 与 008d 同质而非异质。 如果 dt_embedding 是 root cause，我们期望 008f 的分布与 baseline 类似（centered, symmetric）。 但 008f 显示的是 \\\"008d lite\\\"——same direction, smaller magnitude。 这是 \\\"accelerator vs cause\\\" 论证的最强 visual evidence。\\n\\n\\n分布分析会显示：(1) baseline V(s) 与 MC return 高度相关（r=0.92），少量 positive bias（正常）。 (2) 008d 在 collapse 前 V(s) 系统性高于 MC return（82% 的 states 有 positive bias）， 且 bias magnitude 随 training 增长。(3) 008f 在 55K 时也显示类似 pattern（71% positive bias）， 虽然程度较轻。这直接可视化了 RSSM fidelity gap 如何通过 value function 传播： dt=2 imagination 生成 optimistically-biased trajectories → value targets 偏高 → value function learns overestimation → actor exploits overestimated regions。 008f 与 008d 的差异是 degree, not kind——两者都在同一条路上，只是速度不同。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"dt_embedding cosine similarity analysis\",\n    \"description\": \"分析 trained dt_embedding 中 dt=1 vs dt=2 向量的 cosine similarity 演化。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"cosine_sim_init\": 0.15,\n      \"cosine_sim_10K\": 0.35,\n      \"cosine_sim_25K\": 0.08,\n      \"cosine_sim_45K\": -0.12,\n      \"embedding_norm_ratio_dt2_dt1_25K\": 1.4,\n      \"embedding_norm_ratio_dt2_dt1_45K\": 2.1\n    },\n    \"tables\": [],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"dt_embedding 确实学到了 discriminative representation。但在 worst 档叙事下， 这只是 RSSM fidelity gap 被 exploit 的传导通道之一。去掉这个通道（008f）并不消除 exploit——RSSM 的 biased state predictions 本身就是另一个通道。 此分析从 \\\"root cause evidence\\\" 降级为 \\\"mechanism detail of acceleration factor\\\"。\\n\\n\\nTrained dt_embedding 在训练过程中 dt=1 和 dt=2 向量逐渐分离（cosine sim 从 ~0.35 降至 ~-0.12）， 且 dt=2 embedding 的 norm 增大（ratio 从 1.0 增至 2.1x）。这说明 network 学会了 将 dt=2 表示为一个 \\\"amplified, orthogonal\\\" signal，使 value function 可以更精确地 condition on dt。但 precision 的增加恰恰是问题：它使 value function 能更有效地 exploit RSSM 在 dt=2 上的 systematic prediction bias。 然而在 worst 档的 reframed 叙事下，这个分析变得不太重要——dt_embedding 的行为只是 RSSM fidelity gap 被 exploit 的 one channel among many。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Hopper Hop validation (3 seeds × 3 configs)\",\n    \"description\": \"第三个 DMC environment。3 configs: baseline, trained dt_emb, no dt_emb。 Worst 档：进一步确认 temporal abstraction 全面失败。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"baseline_asymptotic\": 220,\n      \"trained_dtEmb_peak\": 95,\n      \"trained_dtEmb_65K\": 55,\n      \"no_dtEmb_peak\": 105,\n      \"no_dtEmb_65K\": 70,\n      \"trained_dtEmb_vs_baseline\": \"-75%\",\n      \"no_dtEmb_vs_baseline\": \"-68%\",\n      \"trained_dtEmb_collapse_rate\": \"2/3\",\n      \"no_dtEmb_collapse_rate\": \"1/3\"\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Hopper Hop summary (3 environments comparison)\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"environment\",\n          \"baseline\",\n          \"trained_dtEmb_best\",\n          \"no_dtEmb_best\",\n          \"dtEmb_effect_size\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"Walker Walk\",\n            950,\n            \"485 (51%)\",\n            \"207 (22%)\",\n            \"~29%\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Cheetah Run\",\n            780,\n            \"420 (54%)\",\n            \"400 (51%)\",\n            \"~3%\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Hopper Hop\",\n            220,\n            \"95 (43%)\",\n            \"105 (48%)\",\n            \"~5%\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"三个 environments 的共同发现：dt>1 全面退化 (remaining performance 22-54% of baseline)。 dt_embedding 的 effect size 在 Walker 之外几乎消失。这是 worst 档叙事的最终 nail： dt_embedding 在 Walker Walk 上 \\\"看起来\\\" 是 root cause，只是因为该 environment 碰巧 对 conditioning mechanism 敏感。在其他 environments 中，RSSM fidelity ceiling 才是 dominant factor，dt_embedding 有无几乎不影响结果。 论文必须以 RSSM fidelity ceiling 作为 central finding，dt_embedding 降级为 Walker-specific secondary effect。\\n\\n\\nHopper Hop 是 DMC 中难度较高的 task，baseline performance 本身较低 (~220)。 dt=2 带来的退化更严重（~70-75% degradation），因为 Hopper 的 hopping dynamics 涉及极其精确的 timing——phase-locked leg movements 和 ground contact 事件。 跳过一个 timestep 意味着完全错过一个 contact event，RSSM 无法从 latent state alone reconstruct 这些信息。trained vs no dt_emb 的差异很小（~7%），与 Cheetah 一致， 进一步证实 RSSM fidelity ceiling 是 environment-general 的。 三个 environments 一致性地显示：dt_embedding 的 effect size 远小于 RSSM 的 dt>1 penalty。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Walker Walk exp_008e_v3 (subsample ON, fixed dt=1, H=15) — continued\",\n    \"description\": \"008e_v3 当前 RUNNING @45K。subsample ON + dt=1 imagination + H=15。 测试 subsample ON 本身的 learning signal reduction effect。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"eval_return_55K\": 430,\n      \"eval_return_65K\": 490,\n      \"eval_return_105K\": 680,\n      \"normalized_ve_55K\": 0.9,\n      \"normalized_ve_65K\": 0.82,\n      \"vs_baseline_105K\": \"-28%\",\n      \"trend\": \"slow convergence, no collapse; reaches ~72% baseline by 105K\"\n    },\n    \"tables\": [],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"008e_v3 是 reframed paper 中的关键 control：它证明 subsample ON + dt=1 imagination 虽然更慢但最终 converge reasonably well。将 imagination dt 从 1 改为 2 才是 catastrophic change——直接指向 RSSM 的 multi-step prediction quality 作为 bottleneck。\\n\\ndt=1 imagination 意味着 RSSM prediction quality 正常（no fidelity gap）， 但 subsample ON 减少了 transitions per episode。在 worst 档下，这个实验反而 表现不错（~72% baseline @105K），证明 subsample ON 本身只是 \\\"fewer data, slower learning\\\" 而非致命问题。这使得 008d/008f 的 collapse 更明确地归因于 dt=2 imagination （而非 subsample ON 的数据减少），进一步支持 RSSM fidelity ceiling 论证。\\n\"\n  }\n]","numLines":725,"startLine":1,"totalLines":725}}}
